# Family and home (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7, the family theme): chains. One of a family says what's on their
# mind (talk.family), the other answers as they are, and sometimes the first has the last word. The answers are
# concepts of their own, so each is the answerer's best rule:
#
#   family.worry_answer   answering a worry; pair.mem.f7_worry says which (money, shop, watch, worn, roofless, damp,
#                         noise, child, child_fret, hurt_you, hurt_me, grief, kin, move, death)
#   family.tease_answer   answering a tease or grumble; pair.mem.f7_tease (chore, duty, spend, kin, envy, pups, dare,
#                         ale, snap, flirt, jibe)
#   family.share_answer   answering news, a memory, a plan, a fond word; pair.mem.f7_share, or self.mem.f7_asked when a
#                         friend asked after their family
#   family.answer_parent  a son or daughter answering their mother or father; pair.mem.f7_pc
#   family.answer_child   a mother or father answering their son or daughter; pair.mem.f7_cp
#   family.settle         the opener's last word, on the tone of the answer: pair.mem.f7_chain (worry, tease, share,
#                         pc, cp) and pair.mem.f7_tone (kind, sharp, jest, fret, eager), set by the answer
#
# A chain's later beats take only the best tier, so every reply keyed to what was said has priority 1: it always
# outranks the replies by temper or humour alone, which are kept for openers that set no key. An answer with no tone
# of its own ends the talk; one that hands on to family.settle remembers its tone.
#
# Careful with names: between spouses, the one spoken to is #dear# or #pet#; #self.child# is the speaker's child, and
# lines about a small one need the parent young enough (self.age<=36) for the child to be a pup. Everyday remarks keep
# a cooldown of a day or two, serious ones half a day. (A rule's `say` can't take ^m/^f: those work in grammar only, so
# a line for one sex is a rule of its own, with other.sex or self.sex.)

# =============================================================================================== Spouses: worries

rule f7_sp_rent
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say Rent's due on Restday and the jar's light, #dear#. | I counted the jar twice. It came out the same both times. | We're short for the rent again. Not by much. By enough. | The landlord stopped me on the stair. Smiling. I don't like it when he smiles.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=money 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_rent_home
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.wealth=poor|destitute here.place=home here.time=dusk|night
cooldown 2d
say Don't light the second candle. We'll manage with one. | I watered the soup. Don't tell me you can taste it. | The landlord's boy was at the door. I said you were out. | I've had the jar out again. It doesn't fill by looking at it.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=money 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_owes
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.owes=yes
cooldown 2d
say I saw the one we owe in the street. I crossed over. | How long can we keep putting them off, #dear#? | I had a letter about the debt. I've not opened it. It's under the bread crock. | They want it by the new month. All of it.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=money 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_dole
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.on_dole=yes
cooldown 2d
say I queued for the parish bread. Don't say anything. | Two hours in the line for one loaf. One. | The priest looked at me kindly. I nearly threw the loaf at him. | Our old neighbour was in the dole line. We both pretended not to see.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=money 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_hungry
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.hungry=yes self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 1d
say There's nothing in the pot but water and hope. | You have the heel of the loaf. I'm not hungry. I'm not. | I could eat the table. We may have to. | I dreamt of a ham. A whole ham. I woke up chewing the blanket.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=money 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_failing
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.business=failing
cooldown 1d
priority 1
say Not one customer today. Not one. | I did the sums. Then I did them again, hoping. | If the shop goes, what do we do? Truly? | I've stock going stale on the shelf and nobody through the door.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=shop 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_guard
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.role=guard
cooldown 2d
say Night watch again this week. | There was a knife out by the gate today. I'm fine. I'm fine. | The captain wants more of us on the walls. | A drunk took a swing at me. Missed. Mostly.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=watch 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_worn
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.tired=yes self.working=yes
cooldown 2d
say I can't keep these hours, #dear#. Something has to give. | I fell asleep standing up today. Standing! | My paws are worn to the pads. | Dawn to dark, and they want me in early tomorrow.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=worn 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_homeless
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.homeless=yes
cooldown 12h
priority 1
say Another night in a doorway, #dear#. Lie close. | I found a barn with half a roof. It's something. | Don't look at me like that. We'll have a door again. | They moved us on from the chapel porch. Kindly, but they moved us on.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=roofless 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_sump_damp
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.quarter=sump
cooldown 2d
say The damp's in the bedding again. | Water came under the door in the night. My boots are swimming. | The rats have found the meal sack. Again. | There's green on the wall behind the bed. Green, #dear#.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=damp 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_nervy_night
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.temper=nervy here.time=night
cooldown 1d
say Did you bar the door? Are you sure? | What was that? Listen. | I heard someone on the stair. I did. | Something's scratching at the shutter. Don't laugh.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=noise 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_child_worry
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.child self.age<=40
cooldown 2d
say #self.child# hardly ate a thing at #supper#. | Did #self.child# seem quiet to you? Too quiet? | #self.child# came home with a split lip and won't say who. | #self.child# lied to me today. Looked me in the eye and lied.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=child 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_child_worry_nervy
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.child self.temper=nervy self.age<=40
cooldown 2d
say #self.child# is late. #self.child# is never late. | Is #self.child# warm enough, do you think? That blanket's thin. | I keep dreaming #self.child# falls in the river. | #self.child# was coughing in the night. Did you hear?
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=child_fret 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_child_grown
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.child self.age>=48
cooldown 3d
say #self.child# hasn't been round in a fortnight. | Do you think #self.child# is happy? Truly? | I saw #self.child# at the market. Thin, I thought. | #self.child# never asks us for anything. I wish they would.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=child 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_hurt
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses other.injured=light|bad
cooldown 6h
priority 1
say Sit down. Let me see it. | You're limping. Don't tell me you're not. | Who did this to you? | Hold still. I'll bind it.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=hurt_you 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_hurt_self
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.injured=bad
cooldown 6h
priority 2
say Help me to the chair, #dear#. Slowly. | I'll be no use at work for days. | Don't fuss. Well. Fuss a bit. | I can't get my boot off. Will you?
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=hurt_me 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_grief
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.mourning=kin
cooldown 6h
priority 3
say I keep waiting for the door to open. | I can't do the funeral things. I can't. | Hold me a while. Don't say anything. | I found their old scarf in the chest. It still smells of them.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=grief 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_grief_friend
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.mourning=friend
cooldown 12h
priority 1
say I keep thinking of the last thing I said to them. It was about the weather. | We were meant to drink together at the festival. | Funny. I'd not seen them in a month, and now I miss them every hour. | I owed them a jar. I'll never pay it now.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=grief 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_mother_ill
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.mother
cooldown 2d
say I should look in on #mum#. She sounded chesty. | #mum.capitalize# says she's fine. She always says she's fine. | I'm worried about #mum# on those stairs. | #mum.capitalize# gave away her good shawl. She's never given away anything.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=kin 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_father_old
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.father
cooldown 2d
say #dad.capitalize# forgot my name yesterday. Just for a breath. | #dad.capitalize# won't stop working. He'll drop where he stands. | Should #dad# come and live with us? | #dad.capitalize# was out in the yard at midnight, looking for a goat he had as a pup.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=kin 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_restless
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.drive=restless
cooldown 3d
say What if we went? Somewhere new. Just packed and went. | I can't spend my whole life on this street, #dear#. | They say there's work in the other towns. Land, even. | A carter said there's houses going cheap down south. Houses, #dear#.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=move 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sp_old_death
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.stage=old other.stage=old world.death=recent
cooldown 3d
say Another one gone. Promise me you'll go second. | When it's my turn, don't let them sing that dreary hymn. | Which of us will it be first, do you think? | We're running out of friends to bury. Then it's us.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=death 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

# =============================================================================================== Spouses: teasing and bickering

rule f7_sp_inlaw_mother
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses other.mother
cooldown 2d
say #other.mother# came by. She moved all the pots. | Your mother asked when we're giving her more grandpups. In the street. | #other.mother# says I put too much salt in. To my face. | #other.mother# brought us a cushion. She says ours are a disgrace.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=kin 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_inlaw_father
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses other.father
cooldown 2d
say #other.father# told me how to hold a broom. A broom. | Your father's been telling everyone at the well about his knee. Everyone. | #other.father# shook my paw today. Like he meant it, for once. | #other.father# called me by your old sweetheart's name. Twice.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=kin 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_short_door
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.temper=short here.place=home
cooldown 2d
say Who left the door wide open? Were you raised in a field? | Mud. On the floor. Paw-shaped mud. | Is it so hard to put the knife back where it lives? | You've hung your wet cloak on my chair. My chair.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=chore 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_chores
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.place=home
cooldown 2d
say It was your turn on the water. Yesterday too. | The shutter's still hanging off. Since spring. | I scrubbed the step. Did you notice? You didn't notice. | You said you'd mend the chair. The chair remembers.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=chore 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_winter_feet
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.season=winter here.place=home
cooldown 2d
say Put your cold feet anywhere but on me. | You've had the blanket all night. All of it. | The fire's out and it was your turn to bank it. | You let the cold in every time you go out to the yard. Every time.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=chore 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_summer_fur
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.season=summer here.place=home
cooldown 2d
say You're shedding on everything. The bread had fur in it. | Don't lie so close, it's like sleeping by an oven. | Brush yourself outside, I'm begging you. | There's more of your coat on the bed than on you.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=chore 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_dawn_snore
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.time=dawn here.place=home
cooldown 2d
say You were snoring again. Like a saw through wet wood. | You talked in your sleep. Who's Hettie? | You kicked me twice. I counted. | You were chasing something in your sleep. Your legs were going like a pup's.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=chore 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_rich_spend
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say You've ordered new hangings for the front room? Again? | You spent how much on that brooch? | The silversmith sent his bill. I want to know what we bought. | Another horse. We've four. You ride one.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=spend 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_heights_dinner
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.quarter=heights
cooldown 2d
say We're asked to dine with the Ashcombes again. Do try to be pleasant. | Lady Ashcombe will be there. Don't mention her nephew. Or her teeth. | And this time, no talk of drains at the table. | The Vanes are giving a musical evening. We're going. Both of us. Awake.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=duty 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_house
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.house
cooldown 3d
say The House expects us at the head's table on the festival. Both of us. Smiling. | Your cousin's steward now. We'll have to call and congratulate them. In person. | We're to wear the House's colours at the festival. Don't argue. | The steward wants us both at the counting of the year. Best coats.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=duty 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_chapel
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.piety=devout other.piety=ordinary here.day=rest
cooldown 3d
say You'll come to chapel with me. Won't you? | The priest asked after you. Kindly. Pointedly. | One hour on Restday, #dear#. The gods give us all the others. | They're blessing the new bell today. Everyone will be there. Everyone.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=duty 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_short_tired
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.temper=short self.tired=yes
cooldown 2d
say Don't. Whatever it is, not now. | If one more person asks me for something today. | I'm going to sit here, and nobody is going to speak. | Every wolf in this town wanted something of me today. Every one.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=snap 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_tavern
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.place=tavern
cooldown 2d
say One more and then home. One. | You've had three. I've been counting even if you haven't. | Slow down. You'll be singing next, and nobody wants that. | That's your last. I'm telling the keeper.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=ale 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_merry
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.humour=merry
cooldown 2d
say Marry me. | Remind me, did I marry you for your looks or your cooking? | If you were a pie, I'd eat you. | Run away with me. Not far. Just to the tavern. | Dance with me. Here. Nobody's looking. Everybody's looking.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=flirt 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_dry
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.humour=dry
cooldown 2d
say You were snoring so loud the neighbours paid us a call. | I've decided to forgive you. For what, I'll think of later. | I'm told marriage is a partnership. Which part's yours? | I've been married to you so long I've started agreeing with you. It's alarming.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=jibe 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_from_apart
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses pair.same_from=no
cooldown 3d
say You said it again. That word from your home. | Your lot eat that with honey? Truly? | Sometimes I can't understand a word your family says. | You still say it the old way, you know. After all these years.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=jibe 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sp_old_tease
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.age>=40 other.age>=40
cooldown 3d
say You were a terror when you were young. You still are. | I found a grey hair. On you, I mean. Mine are silver. | Twenty years and you still leave the lid off the crock. | Would you marry me again? Think carefully.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=jibe 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

# =============================================================================================== Spouses: fond words, news and plans

rule f7_sp_old_years
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.stage=old other.stage=old
cooldown 2d
say All those years. Where did they go? | Do you remember the day we met? You had mud to the knees. | Do you remember our first winter? One blanket and a leaking roof. | We've buried a lot of friends, you and me. Still here, though.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=years 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_old_paws
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.stage=old other.stage=old here.time=dusk|night
cooldown 2d
say Give me your paw. There. Just like that. | Sit by me a while. The pots can wait. | Come and sit. Let's watch the fire go down. | Lean on me. There. That's better.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=tender 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_middle
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.stage=adult other.stage=adult self.age>=40
cooldown 3d
say Do you ever think about how fast it all went? | Do you remember the year we nearly lost the house? | Remember when we thought this house was big? | Half our lives under one roof. Imagine that.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=years 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_wedding_news
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses world.wedding=recent
cooldown 3d
say All this wedding talk. Remember ours? | Their wedding had a fiddler. Ours had your uncle singing. | They looked so young up there. Were we ever that young? | The bride cried all through the vows. You laughed all through ours.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=years 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_young
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.age<=26 other.age<=26
cooldown 2d
say I still can't get used to your boots by my door. Our door. | I woke and forgot we were married. Then I remembered. Good morning. | My mother asked if you snore. I said I'd not noticed. I've noticed. | Our name's on the rent book. Both of us. Did you see?
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=newlywed 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_young_home
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.age<=26 other.age<=26 here.place=home
cooldown 2d
say I burned the porridge. Our first burned porridge. | We need a second chair. People will think we're poor. | Where do we keep the salt? Where do we keep anything? | We've a shelf of our own. One shelf. I keep looking at it.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=newlywed 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_proud_child
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.child self.age<=36
cooldown 2d
say Did you see #self.child# carry the water in? Both buckets! | #self.child# said thank you to the baker without being told. | #self.child#'s got your stubborn streak. Don't smile. | #self.child# shared the honey cake with the little one next door. Unasked.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=proud_child 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_thriving
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.business=thriving
cooldown 2d
say We should take on a second pair of paws. | Sold out by noon. I nearly hugged the last customer. | We could put something by this year. Real savings. | I paid every bill on the day it came. Every one. I felt like a lord.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=good 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_ambitious
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.drive=ambitious
cooldown 3d
say A bigger place by spring. I mean it. | I've an eye on the empty shop on the corner. | We won't always be counting pennies. Not if I can help it. | Give me five years and they'll be calling us by name in the market.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=plan 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_content
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.drive=content
cooldown 3d
say A warm fire, a full pot, and you. What else is there? | I wouldn't change a thing. Well. The roof. | This is enough, isn't it? It's enough for me. | Some folk want the world. I want this chair and you in the other one.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=content 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_dayoff
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.shift=day_off
cooldown 2d
say A whole day. What shall we do with it? | No work, no callers. What's it to be? | The day's ours. Name it. | Nobody needs us till tomorrow. What do you fancy?
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=dayoff 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_tired_evening
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.tired=yes here.time=dusk|night
cooldown 2d
say Rub my shoulders and I'll love you forever. | I'm asleep. This is me talking in my sleep. | #supper.capitalize#, then #bed#, then nothing at all. | My tail's too heavy to lift. That's how tired.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=tired 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_birth_news
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses world.birth=recent self.parent=no self.age<=40
cooldown 3d
say Did you see the new pup on the street? Tiny paws. I held one. | Do you ever think about one of our own? | The whole street's gone soft over that new pup. Me too. | I knitted a little cap for the new pup. Then I thought, what if it were ours?
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=pups_wish 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_festival
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.day=festival here.festival
cooldown 2d
say Dance with me at #here.festival#. Just one. | Wear the blue for #here.festival#. You look well in the blue. | Let's stay out till the lamps go. It's #here.festival#. | We'll eat everything at #here.festival#. Everything. Then dance it off.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=fest 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_market
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.day=market
cooldown 2d
say What do we need? I had a list and I've lost it. | Don't buy anything with a ribbon on it. | Meet me at the bread stall at noon. | I've four pennies for the market. Spend them wisely. Spend them on me.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=market 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_rain
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.weather=rain|storm
cooldown 2d
say Let's not go out. Let's stay in and let it pour. | The roof's holding. Mostly. Put the pot under the corner. | Listen to it on the shutters. I love that sound. | Nobody's coming to the door in this. It's just us.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=cosy 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_snow
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.weather=snow
cooldown 2d
say Snowed in, near enough. Just us and the fire. | Your nose is frozen. Come here. | Look at it come down. The whole street's gone quiet. | We're not going anywhere today. I've decided.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=cosy 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_far_home
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.from!=ridgemere pair.same_from=yes here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 3d
say I dreamt of home last night. The old home. | This city's never quiet, is it? Not once. | Do you think we'll ever go back? Even for a visit? | I heard someone in the market talk like our folk. I nearly wept.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=far_home 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_city_miss
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.from=ridgemere here.region!=ridgemere
cooldown 3d
say I miss the city some days. The noise, even. | You'd never get bread like this in Ridgemere. I'll give it that. | I keep listening for the harbour bell. There's no harbour bell. | Some nights I'd give a week's pay for a pie off a Ridgemere cart.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=city_miss 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_small
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses
cooldown 1d
say I saw your cousin at the well. She's let her fur go. | I was thinking about you today. Nothing bad. | I've lost a sock. I suspect you. | The neighbour's goat ate a sleeve off my washing. One sleeve. | A bird got in the chimney. It's still there, I think. Singing.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=small 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sp_supper
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.time=day|dusk
cooldown 1d
say What shall we have for #supper#? | What do you fancy tonight? | I've a mind to cook something special tonight. Any wishes? | Shall I fetch something in for #supper#, or will you?
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=supper 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

# =============================================================================================== Parents to their children
# The opener remembers what kind of remark it was (pair.mem.f7_pc), so the son or daughter answers that
# (family.answer_parent), and the parent may have the last word on the tone of it (family.settle).

rule f7_pc_young_order
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say Show me your paws. Both of them. | Boots off at the door. Off. | Fetch the kindling in before dark. | Wash behind your ears. Both ears. I'll be checking.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=order 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_river
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young
cooldown 2d
say Don't you dare go near the river today. | Stay where I can see you. | Not past the well, mind. Not one step past. | If the big ones go down to the water, you come home.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=warn 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_ask
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say What did you learn today? | Who've you been playing with? | What did you do all day, then? | Did anything happen at the well today?
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=ask 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_mess
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say Why is there a frog in the washtub? | Where did all that mud come from? | Who's been at the honey? There's a paw print in it. | Why is the cat wearing my scarf?
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=mess 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_poor
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say No sweets this week, pup. Next market day, maybe. | No new boots till spring. Make these last. | No honey this week. We'll have some at the festival. | We can't have the fair this year, pup. Next year.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=without 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_hungry
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young self.hungry=yes
cooldown 1d
priority 1
say Here, have mine. I ate earlier. | You finish it. I'm not hungry. | Eat up. I had mine on the way home. | Have the last of the bread. Go on. I'm full.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=food 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_rich
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young self.wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say Your tutor says you drew whiskers on the lessons again. Stop it. | You'll greet the guests and then you'll go upstairs. Quietly. | Don't play with the stable pups in your good clothes. | Stand up straight when the steward speaks to you.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=manners 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_sump
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young self.quarter=sump
cooldown 2d
say Stay off the steps by the water after dark. | Don't talk to the ones by the old warehouse. Ever. | If anyone offers you anything, you run home. | If you find a purse in the gutter, you leave it in the gutter.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=warn 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_docks
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young self.quarter=docks|wharf|harbour_hill
cooldown 2d
say Keep away from the ropes when they're loading. | Don't you go aboard anything. Not for a dare, not for anything. | If a sailor gives you a sweet, give it back. | Stay off the end of the pier. The planks are rotten.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=warn 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_short
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young self.temper=short
cooldown 2d
say What did I say about the mud? What did I say? | Inside. Now. I'm not asking twice. | Put that down. No. Down. | Stop that whining this instant.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=order 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_merry
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young self.humour=merry
cooldown 2d
say Who's this stranger at my table? Oh! It's you. You've grown a whole tail. | I'll race you home. Loser washes the pots. | Eat your greens and you'll grow ears like mine. Enormous. | Is that a pup or a mud pie? I can't tell. I'll have to taste it.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=play 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_devout
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young self.piety=devout here.day=rest
cooldown 2d
say Paws washed. We're going to chapel. | Sit still in chapel today and there's honey after. | Say your thanks before you eat. All of them. | Best collar on. It's Restday.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=chapel 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_work
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young self.shift=before
cooldown 1d
say I'm off to work. Be good till I'm home. | Bar the door behind me. And no fire till I'm back. | I'll be home before dark. Mind the house. | Off I go. Don't let the neighbour's goat in.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=goodbye 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_grief
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young self.mourning=kin
cooldown 6h
priority 3
say Come here. Just sit with me a while. | It's all right to cry. I am. | They loved you very much. You know that? | You can talk about them, you know. Any time. I like to hear it.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=grief 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_young_night
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young here.time=night
cooldown 1d
say Eyes shut. I can see them open from here. | That was the last story. The very last. | Into bed. Tail and all. | Stop wriggling. Sleep comes to the still ones.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=bed 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_teen_trade
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=adolescent other.apprentice=no
cooldown 3d
say Have you given any thought to a trade? | The cooper wants a pair of paws. Will you go and see him? | You can't sit about forever. What do you want to do? | I spoke to the smith. He'd look at you, if you asked nicely.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=trade 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_teen_master
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.apprentice=yes
cooldown 2d
say How's your master treating you? | Are you minding what you're told at the shop? | You look worn out. Are they working you too hard? | Has your master let you near the real work yet?
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=master 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_teen_night
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=adolescent here.time=night
cooldown 2d
say Where were you till this hour? | Who was that walking you to the door? | I've been sat up waiting. Where were you? | The lamps were lit an hour ago. Where have you been?
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=late 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_teen_short
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=adolescent self.temper=short
cooldown 2d
say Take that look off your face. | You'll speak to me properly under my roof. | Your room. Now. It's a midden. | Don't you sigh at me.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=scold 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_teen_restless
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=adolescent other.drive=restless|ambitious
cooldown 3d
say I know you're itching to be off. I was too. | The world's not going anywhere. It'll wait a year. | Don't be in such a hurry to leave us. | You've had your eyes on that road all summer. Don't think I haven't seen.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=leave 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_teen_heights
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=adolescent self.quarter=heights
cooldown 3d
say The Ashcombes' youngest would make a sound match. Think of the families. | You'll dance with whoever you're asked to dance with at the ball. | Your marriage isn't only yours, you know. It never is, up here. | The Vanes have asked after you. Twice. That means something, up here.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=match 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_teen_poor
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=adolescent self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 3d
say You'll need to bring in some coin soon. I'm sorry. | Ask at the inn. They take on youngsters for the carrying. | I wanted you to have longer before you worked. I did. | There's day work going at the edge of town. It's hard, but it pays.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=earn 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_teen_order
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=adolescent
cooldown 1d
say Your room smells like a wet badger. Open a shutter. | Help your #gran# with the stairs. | Home before the lamps, and I mean before. | Those boots go by the door, not on the table.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=order 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_teen_ask
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adult|old other.stage=adolescent
cooldown 1d
say Talk to me. What's going on in that head? | Who's this friend you keep going on about? | You've been quiet all week. What is it? | You've not eaten properly in days. What's the matter?
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=ask_teen 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_adult_grandpups
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent pair.elder=a self.stage=old other.stage=adult other.parent=no other.married=yes
cooldown 3d
say When are you giving me grandpups? I'm not getting younger. | Your cousin's on her third. Just saying. | I've knitted a little blanket. No reason. | I've kept your old cradle. It's in the loft. Just mentioning it.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=grandpups 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_adult_grandchild
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent pair.elder=a self.stage=old other.child
cooldown 2d
say Bring #other.child# round on Restday. I've saved the honey. | #other.child# has your ears. And mine, come to that. | Is #other.child# eating properly? You never did. | I've a story for #other.child#. A long one, with a bear in it.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=grandpup 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_adult_widowed
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent pair.elder=a self.stage=old self.widowed=yes
cooldown 2d
say I set out two cups again this morning. | The bed's too big. Isn't that silly? | I keep saving them the warm side of the fire. | I found their old tin whistle in the chest. I can't play it. I keep it anyway.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=lonely 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_adult_hurt
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent pair.elder=a self.stage=old self.injured=light|bad
cooldown 1d
say My hip's playing up. Don't make a face. | I took a tumble on the step. It's nothing. It's something. | The healer says rest. I say rubbish. | I can't get down the stairs without the rail now. There. I've said it.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=hurt 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_adult_help
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent pair.elder=a self.wealth=rich|comfortable other.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 3d
say Let me help with the rent. Don't argue. | I put something in your coat pocket. Don't look. | There's a sack of meal by the door. It's yours. | I've paid the cobbler for your boots. Go and fetch them.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=help 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_adult_unwed_son
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent pair.elder=a self.stage=old other.stage=adult other.married=no other.sex=male
cooldown 3d
say Has anyone caught your eye? | The miller's daughter asked after you. Asked twice. | You can't marry your work, you know. | There's a nice girl at chapel who laughs at everything. You could use that.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=match 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_adult_unwed_daughter
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent pair.elder=a self.stage=old other.stage=adult other.married=no other.sex=female
cooldown 3d
say Has anyone caught your eye? | The miller's son asked after you. Asked twice. | You can't marry your work, you know. | The cooper's boy has a good trade and all his teeth. Just saying.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=match 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_pc_adult_fret
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent pair.elder=a self.stage=old other.stage=adult
cooldown 1d
say You look thin. Are you eating? | You never visit. You're here now. Never mind. | You work too hard. You get that from me. | Is that coat warm enough? It doesn't look warm enough.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=fret 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

# =============================================================================================== Children to their parents
# The opener remembers what kind (pair.mem.f7_cp), so the mother or father answers that (family.answer_child), and
# the son or daughter may have the last word on the tone of it (family.settle).

rule f7_cp_young_why
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=young other.stage=adult|old
cooldown 1d
say Why do we have tails? | Where does the rain go after? | Why do geese honk at nothing? | Why can't I stay up? You stay up. | Why do the old ones smell of cupboards?
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=why 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_young_little
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=young other.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say Were you ever little? Really little? | What were you like when you were my size? | Did you have a #gran# too? | Did you ever get in trouble? Real trouble?
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=little 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_young_poor
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=young self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say Are we poor? Brindle said we're poor. | Why don't I get new boots like the others? | Why do we only have bread? | Tam's family has meat every day. Every day!
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=poor 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_young_hungry
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=young self.hungry=yes
cooldown 1d
priority 1
say My belly's growling. Listen. | Is there anything to eat? Anything? | When's #supper#? Is it soon? Is it now? | I'm so hungry I could eat a whole goose. With the feathers.
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=hungry 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_young_night
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=young here.time=night
cooldown 1d
say Can I sleep in your bed? There's a noise. | Leave the door open. A crack. A bigger crack. | Is there such a thing as the Fen Hag? Really? | Something's under my bed. It breathed.
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=fear 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_young_grief
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=young self.mourning=kin
cooldown 6h
priority 3
say Where did they go? Are they coming back? | Is it my fault? I was naughty that day. | Can I keep their scarf? | Will they still know me when I'm big?
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=grief 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_young_rich
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=young self.wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say Why can't I play by the river with the others? | The cook's pup says we're rich. Are we? What's rich? | Why do I have to go to dancing? The others don't. | Why does the stable pup get to have muddy paws and I don't?
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=rich 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_young_merry
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=young self.humour=merry
cooldown 2d
say I've got a frog in my pocket. His name's Sir. | I can whistle! Nearly. Listen. | I told a joke at the well and everybody laughed. Even the old ones. | I can make my ears go flat and up and flat. Look!
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=news 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_young_want
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say Can I have a hen of my own? I'll feed it. | Can I have a penny? I'll give it back. One day. | I found a beetle. Can it live with us? | Can I go and play at the well? Please?
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=want 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_young_news
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say When I'm big I'm going to be a guard. Or a baker. Or both. | I found a stone with a hole in it. It's lucky. | The baker's cat licked me. On the nose. | I can count to a hundred. Nearly.
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=news 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_teen_leave
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adolescent self.drive=restless|ambitious
cooldown 3d
say I want to go and see the world. There's work out there. Real work. | I'm not a pup any more. I want to see something. Anything. | I'm going to leave one day. You know that, don't you? | The carters say there's places past the hills where nobody knows your name.
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=leave 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_teen_room
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adolescent self.quarter=sump
cooldown 3d
say Can I not have a corner of my own? A curtain, even? | I'm sick of sleeping four to a mattress. | When I've money we're moving up the hill. All of us. | I can hear everything through that wall. Everything.
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=cramped 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_apprentice
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.apprentice=yes other.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say My master made me sweep the same floor three times. | I made a thing today. A whole thing. It was crooked, but. | I'm going to be better at it than my master one day. | My master said "not bad" today. Not bad!
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=work 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_teen_want
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adolescent
cooldown 1d
say Can I borrow the good cloak? I'll be careful. | Everyone else gets to go to the dance. Everyone. | Can I stay at Fennick's tonight? Their mother says yes. | Can I have my own knife? A proper one?
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=want_teen 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_teen_complain
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent self.stage=adolescent
cooldown 1d
say You're embarrassing me. You're standing there embarrassingly. | Why do you always ask where I'm going? | You never let me do anything. | Don't call me pup in front of people.
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=sulk 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_adult_care
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent pair.elder=b self.stage=adult other.stage=old
cooldown 2d
say You should come and live with us. There's room. | Did you take what the healer gave you? | Let me carry that. Please. Just let me. | I'll do your roof on Restday. Don't argue.
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=care 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_adult_widowed
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent pair.elder=b self.stage=adult other.widowed=yes
cooldown 2d
say Have you eaten today? Properly? | Come for #supper#. Every night, if you like. | I miss them too. Every day. | I walked past the old bench today. Their bench. I sat a while.
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=care_widowed 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_adult_richer
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent pair.elder=b self.stage=adult self.wealth=rich|comfortable other.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 3d
say I've paid your coal for the winter. It's done. Don't argue. | Let me do this. You did everything for me. | I'll not have you queuing for parish bread. Not while I've breath. | I've a purse for you. Don't count it in front of me.
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=help 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_adult_news
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent pair.elder=b self.stage=adult self.child self.age<=36
cooldown 2d
say #self.child# took a step today. Two steps! | #self.child# asked for you by name. | #self.child# bit the neighbour's pup. I don't know where that came from. Yes I do. | #self.child# drew you. You've four ears and a tail like a broom.
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=grandpup 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_cp_adult_work
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=parent pair.elder=b self.stage=adult self.business=thriving|failing
cooldown 2d
say The shop's had a month. I'll tell you about it. | I've been doing the books. I wish I'd listened when you showed me. | You always said trade was a fickle thing. You were right. | I need your advice. About the shop. Don't gloat.
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=shop 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

# =============================================================================================== Brothers and sisters

rule f7_sib_mother
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=siblings self.stage=adult|old self.mother
cooldown 2d
say Have you been to see #mum#? She says you haven't. | #mum.capitalize#'s sorted the attic. She found your drawings. | #mum.capitalize# asked me which of us is her favourite. I said you. To be kind. | #mum.capitalize#'s taken against the baker. Don't ask. Just don't buy his bread.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=our_mother 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sib_father_worry
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=siblings self.stage=adult|old self.father
cooldown 2d
say #dad.capitalize#'s worse. He won't say, but he's worse. | Somebody should talk to #dad# about the stairs. Somebody meaning you. | #dad.capitalize# gave me his old knife. He's giving his things away. That's not like him. | #dad.capitalize# couldn't remember the way home from the well.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=kin 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_sib_richer
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=siblings self.stage=adult|old pair.richer=a
cooldown 3d
say If you're short, you only have to say. | I heard about your roof. Let me send someone. | You're too proud to ask. You always were. | There's a coat at mine that doesn't fit me. It'd fit you.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=offer 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sib_poorer
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=siblings self.stage=adult|old pair.richer=b
cooldown 3d
say Nice coat. New, is it? | I suppose you'll be too grand for us at the festival. | Could you... no. Never mind. | #mum.capitalize# always did say you'd go far. She didn't say you'd forget us.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=envy 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sib_young
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=siblings self.stage=young|adolescent other.stage=young|adolescent
cooldown 1d
say I'm telling #mum#. | That's mine. I had it first. | You've got jam on your ear. | You smell like the goat. | You've been in my box. Don't lie.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=pups 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sib_dare
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=siblings self.stage=young other.stage=young|adolescent
cooldown 2d
say Bet you can't climb the wall. | I dare you to knock on old Marrow's door and run. | Race you to the well. Loser's a toad. | Bet you can't hold your breath till the cart's gone by.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=dare 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sib_adult_memory
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=siblings self.stage=adult|old other.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say Remember when we hid in the woodpile and they called the watch? | Do you remember the winter we had the one pair of boots between us? | I passed the old house. Somebody's painted the door blue. | Remember #dad#'s face when you brought the goat home?
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=sib_memory 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_sib_adult_jibe
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=siblings self.stage=adult|old other.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say You still owe me for the good bowl. | You've gone grey at the muzzle. When did that happen? | You've got #dad#'s laugh now. It's unsettling. | You still eat like a pup. Elbows everywhere.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=jibe 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_sib_mourning
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=siblings self.mourning=kin self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 6h
priority 3
say We're the old ones now, you and me. | I keep thinking of us as pups, all of us round the table. | Who's going to sort their things? I can't. I can't yet. | I went to tell them something today. Got halfway there.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=grief 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

# =============================================================================================== Kin and the household

rule f7_hh_plain
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=household
cooldown 1d
say It was your turn on the water. Again. | Your snoring comes through the wall like a cart. | Somebody's been at my bread. I marked it. | You left the door on the latch all night.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=chore 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_hh_rent
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=household self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say Have you got your share of the rent? I'm short myself. | The landlord says he's raising it at the new month. | If one of us goes, the other can't make the rent alone. | I've sold my good knife for the rent. Don't ask me to do it again.
then other: family.worry_answer
remember pair: f7_worry=money 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=worry 2m

rule f7_hh_sump
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=household self.quarter=sump
cooldown 2d
say The bucket's full again. Your turn to carry it down. | You used the last of the lamp oil. Again. | Your washing's dripping on my bed. | You let the rats in. Door wide open, half the night.
then other: family.tease_answer
remember pair: f7_tease=chore 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=tease 2m

rule f7_kin_old_young
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=family self.stage=old other.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say Come and sit by me. I've a story for you. | Shall I tell you what your father got up to at your age? Worse than you. | Shall I tell you about the winter the river froze? | Come here. I've a secret, and it's only for you.
then other: family.answer_parent
remember pair: f7_pc=story 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=pc 2m

rule f7_kin_young_gran
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=family self.stage=young other.stage=old other.sex=female
cooldown 1d
say #gran.capitalize#, tell me the one about the wolf in the well. | Can I have one of your sweets? The red ones? | #gran.capitalize#, can I sit on your lap? Just for a bit? | Can I brush your tail, #gran#? I'll be gentle.
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=gran 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_kin_young_grandad
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=family self.stage=young other.stage=old other.sex=male
cooldown 1d
say #grandad.capitalize#, tell me the one about the wolf in the well. | Can I have one of your sweets? The red ones? | #grandad.capitalize#, can I sit on your lap? Just for a bit? | Can I wear your hat, #grandad#? Just round the room?
then other: family.answer_child
remember pair: f7_cp=gran 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=cp 2m

rule f7_kin_festival
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=family self.stage=adult|old here.day!=festival
cooldown 3d
say Is your lot coming to us for the festival, or are we going to you? | Who's having everyone this festival? I've done it twice running. | Somebody has to have the whole family this festival. I had them last time. | Where are we all eating at the festival? Somebody decide.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=gathering 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_kin_trouble
when concept=talk.family pair.kin=family self.stage=adult|old other.stage=adult|old
cooldown 3d
say Your brother still owes my brother a pig. | I heard about the trouble at yours. I hope it's sorted. | Our aunt's not speaking to your aunt. Again. Nobody knows why. | Somebody told Gran about the broken jug. It wasn't me. Mostly.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=kin_trouble 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

# =============================================================================================== Asking after each other's families (friends, acquaintances)

rule f7_ask_spouse
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.friends|talk.day pair.band=friends|acquaintances other.spouse
cooldown 2d
say And how's #other.spouse# keeping? | Give my best to #other.spouse#. Is all well there? | I saw #other.spouse# at the market. Looking well, I thought. | Is #other.spouse# still putting up with you?
then other: family.share_answer
remember other: f7_asked=spouse 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_ask_child
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.friends|talk.day pair.band=friends|acquaintances other.child other.age<=36
cooldown 2d
say How's young #other.child#? | Is #other.child# behaving? | #other.child#'s getting so big. What are you feeding them? | I saw #other.child# chasing geese by the well. Fast, that one.
then other: family.share_answer
remember other: f7_asked=child 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_ask_child_grown
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.friends|talk.day pair.band=friends|acquaintances other.child other.age>=46
cooldown 3d
say How's #other.child# getting on these days? | Do you see much of #other.child#? | I saw #other.child# the other day. The image of you. | Is #other.child# settled yet?
then other: family.share_answer
remember other: f7_asked=child_grown 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_ask_mother
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.friends pair.band=friends other.mother other.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say How's your mother? Still going strong? | Is #other.mother# well? I've not seen her at the well. | Tell #other.mother# I'll bring the jar back. I've not forgotten. | Your mother gave me such a look in the market. What have I done?
then other: family.share_answer
remember other: f7_asked=mother 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_ask_widowed
when concept=talk.friends|talk.day pair.band=friends other.widowed=yes
cooldown 3d
say How are you managing, on your own? | Are you eating? You look thin. | Come to us for #supper#. You shouldn't be alone every night. | I still miss them, you know. I can't think how you must.
then other: family.share_answer
remember other: f7_asked=alone 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_tell_inlaws
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.friends self.spouse
cooldown 3d
say #self.spouse#'s family are coming for the festival. All of them. | My mother-in-law has opinions about my cooking. Loud ones. | We've the in-laws staying. Can I sleep at yours? | #self.spouse#'s brother has borrowed my good saw. For a year now.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=inlaws 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_tell_child_trouble
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.friends self.child self.age<=40
cooldown 3d
say #self.child# wants to go off and see the world. I'm not ready. | #self.child# has a sweetheart. Don't tell anyone I told you. | #self.child# broke a window. With a cabbage. Don't ask me how. | #self.child# brought home a fox cub. It's in the woodshed. It bites.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=child_news 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_tell_childless
when concept=talk.friends self.married=yes self.parent=no self.stage=adult self.age<=40
cooldown 4d
say Everyone asks when we'll have pups. Everyone. | We'd hoped there'd be little ones by now. | It'll happen or it won't. That's what I tell myself. | The midwife looked at me in the street today. Just looked.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=childless 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

rule f7_tell_family_house
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.friends self.house
cooldown 4d
say The House has us all at the head's table this month. Dreadful food. | Everyone in my family works for the House. Cousins, aunts, the cat. | You never get away from the family when the family's the House. | My uncle's been made a steward. We'll never hear the end of it.
then other: family.share_answer
remember pair: f7_share=house_life 2m
remember pair: f7_chain=share 2m

# =============================================================================================== family.worry_answer (self answers the worry)
# Keyed by pair.mem.f7_worry, priority 1, so the right kind of answer always speaks; the tone it remembers chooses the
# opener's last word.

rule f7_wa_plain
when concept=family.worry_answer
say Hm. Let me think on it. | One thing at a time. | We'll see. We'll see.

rule f7_wa_money
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=money
priority 1
say We'll manage. We always have. | Something'll turn up. It always does. | I'll ask about for extra work. | Then we tighten our belts another notch.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_money_warm
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=money self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say Come here. We'll sort it, you and me. | Don't carry it on your own. Give me half. | Whatever comes, it comes to both of us.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_money_poor
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=money self.wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
say I'll ask at the inn for a day's carrying. | We could sell the good pot. We never use it good. | I can go without the ale. I'll go without the ale. | I've a few pennies in my boot. I was saving them. Here.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_money_ambitious
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=money self.drive=ambitious
priority 1
say I'll find more work. I'll find two lots of work. | This won't be us forever. I promise you that. | Next year we'll laugh at this. I'll make sure of it.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_money_short
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=money self.temper=short
priority 1
say If you didn't spend it on ribbons. | Don't look at me. I bring it home. | Then we eat less. Simple. | What do you want, a miracle?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_wa_money_sly
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=money self.honesty=sly
priority 1
say Leave the landlord to me. He owes me a favour. Sort of. | There's ways. Don't ask what ways. | I know a fellow. I always know a fellow.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sly 2m

rule f7_wa_money_dry
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=money self.humour=dry
priority 1
say Well, it can't get worse. Don't quote me. | Good. I was short of things to lie awake over. | Shall I panic now, or after #supper#?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_wa_money_merry
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=money self.humour=merry
priority 1
say Chin up. Nobody ever died of an empty jar. A few came close. | We'll laugh about this. Not yet. But we will. | Poor, but handsome. That's us.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_wa_money_nervy
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=money self.temper=nervy
priority 1
say Oh, don't. Now I'll not sleep either. | I knew it. I knew something was wrong. | What do we do? What do we do?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fret 2m

rule f7_wa_money_comfortable
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=money self.wealth=comfortable|rich
priority 1
say It's a lean month, not a lean life. | We've put by. It's what putting by is for. | Then we go without the cream a while. We'll live.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_money_devout
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=money self.piety=devout
priority 1
say The Bright One's never let us starve yet. | I'll light a candle for it. And then I'll go and find work. | We've a roof today. Give thanks for today.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_shop
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=shop
priority 1
say Something'll turn. Trade always turns. | Then we tighten our belts till it does. | Folk are #skint# everywhere. It's not you. | Put a sign out. A big one. With a pie on it.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_shop_merchant
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=shop self.role=merchant
priority 1
say Sell the stale stock cheap by noon, and start again. | Every shop has a bad season. Mine had three in a row. | Find what the market's short of, and sell that.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_shop_warm
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=shop self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say Whatever happens to the shop, I'm still here. | Shop or no shop, you're the best thing on this street. | We started with nothing. We know how.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_shop_short
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=shop self.temper=short
priority 1
say Then stop moaning and lower your prices. | I said that corner was a bad spot. I said. | Moping at the counter won't bring them in.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_wa_shop_dry
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=shop self.humour=dry
priority 1
say On the bright side, the shelves have never been tidier. | Well, at least nobody's stealing from it. | You could sell tickets to look at the empty shop. Novelty.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_wa_shop_nervy
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=shop self.temper=nervy
priority 1
say What'll we do? What'll we do if it goes? | I've been dreading this. All month I've been dreading it. | Don't say it. If you say it, it'll happen.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fret 2m

rule f7_wa_watch
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=watch
priority 1
say Come home safe. That's all I ask. That's all. | Stand at the back. For me. | I hate that sword. I hate that it's yours. | Promise me you'll not be a hero.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fret 2m

rule f7_wa_watch_dry
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=watch self.humour=dry
priority 1
say Next time let the drunk win. It's quicker. | Tell your captain I'm worse than any knife, and I want you back whole. | Missed mostly. Wonderful. I'll sleep like a pup.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_wa_watch_short
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=watch self.temper=short
priority 1
say Then tell the captain no. You're allowed to say no. | Every week it's something. Every week. | They don't pay you enough to bleed for them.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_wa_watch_devout
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=watch self.piety=devout
priority 1
say I pray every night you're on the walls. Every night. | The Bright One keeps the watch too. I've asked. | I'll light a candle at the gate shrine. Two.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fret 2m

rule f7_wa_worn
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=worn
priority 1
say Then something will give. Not you. | Sit. I'll do #supper#. | Tell them you're a wolf, not a mule. | Sleep. I'll wake you when the pot's hot.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_worn_short
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=worn self.temper=short
priority 1
say Then stop saying yes to everything. | You'll work yourself into the ground, and then where will I be? | I've told you. I've told you a hundred times.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_wa_worn_dry
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=worn self.humour=dry
priority 1
say Standing up! You've learned a trick. They'll want you at the fair. | Worn to the pads. Shall I have you resoled? | Good. You'll sleep through my snoring for once.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_wa_worn_tired
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=worn self.tired=yes
priority 1
say You and me both. Two old boots by the fire, the pair of us. | Sit down before you fall down. I'll sit with you. | I'd rub your feet if I could lift my arms.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_roofless
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=roofless
priority 1
say At least we're together. At least that. | The chapel porch is dry. We'll try there. | One day a door of our own. With a lock. And a step. | Lie close, then. We'll be warm enough.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_roofless_short
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=roofless self.temper=short
priority 1
say Don't. I can't hear it tonight. | I know where we are. I don't need telling. | Save your breath for keeping warm.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_wa_roofless_devout
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=roofless self.piety=devout
priority 1
say The Bright One sees us. Even here. | We'll pray, and then we'll find a barn. In that order. | The gods had no roof either, the old songs say.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_damp
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=damp
priority 1
say I'll stuff the gap with rags. It'll hold till spring. | We've had worse. Remember the first room? | I'll speak to the landlord. Again. | Hang the bedding by the fire. It'll dry. Mostly.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_damp_short
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=damp self.temper=short
priority 1
say And what do you want me to do, drain the Sound? | It's the Sump. It's damp. That's what the Sump is. | Complain to the landlord, not to me.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_wa_damp_dry
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=damp self.humour=dry
priority 1
say Damp's free. It's the one thing round here they don't charge for. | We'll keep fish in the bedding. Save on the fishmonger. | The rats have to eat too, I suppose. Apparently from our sack.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_wa_noise
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=noise
priority 1
say It's the cat from next door. It's always the cat. | I barred it. I barred it twice. Go to sleep. | It's the wind. Listen. There. Wind. | I'll look. Stay here. No, don't come. Fine, come.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_noise_short
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=noise self.temper=short
priority 1
say It's nothing. It's always nothing. Sleep. | If it's a thief, I hope he's quieter than you. | Every night. Every single night.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_wa_noise_dry
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=noise self.humour=dry
priority 1
say If it's a thief, he's welcome to the turnips. | It's a ghost. A very small one. With a mouse's tail. | Whoever it is, they'll find nothing worth the climb.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_wa_noise_nervy
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=noise self.temper=nervy
priority 1
say I heard it too. Don't move. | Get the poker. Quietly. | Shh. There. Again. You heard that?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fret 2m

rule f7_wa_noise_guard
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=noise self.role=guard
priority 1
say I'll look. I do it every night for strangers. I can do it for you. | Stay behind me. If it's anything, it's a cat. | I know every noise this street makes. That's the gutter.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_child
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=child
priority 1
say I'll talk to them tonight. Gently. | They're growing. It takes them strange. | We were the same at that age. Worse. | Leave it a day. If it's still there, we'll ask.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_child_warm
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=child self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say I'll take them fishing. They talk when their paws are busy. | I'll sit with them after #supper#. Just sit. | Leave a candle by the bed. They'll come to us when they're ready.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_child_short
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=child self.temper=short
priority 1
say They'll get a piece of my mind, is what they'll get. | You coddle them. That's what this is. | When I was that age I'd have had a clip round the ear.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_wa_child_grown
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=child self.age>=48
priority 1
say They've their own lives now. It's as it should be. | I'll go round on Restday. With a pie. | They're grown. They'll come to us when they need to. | We did the same to our folks. Worse.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_child_fret
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=child_fret
priority 1
say They're tougher than you think. | You fret enough for the both of us. | I'll look in on them on my way to bed. | Pups are made of leather and noise. They'll do.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_child_fret_nervy
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=child_fret self.temper=nervy
priority 1
say Now you've said it I'll not sleep. I'll go and look. | Should we fetch the healer? Should we? | Oh, gods. I'll check the shutters again.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fret 2m

rule f7_wa_child_fret_short
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=child_fret self.temper=short
priority 1
say Leave them be. You'll smother them. | They're fine. You're the one I'm worried about. | Every night it's something new with you.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_wa_hurt_you
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=hurt_you
priority 1
say It's nothing. A knock. | Don't look at it like that. It looks worse than it is. | Ow. Yes. All right, it's something. | I'll live. Just about.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=brave 2m

rule f7_wa_hurt_you_bad
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=hurt_you self.injured=bad
priority 2
say I can't feel my paw, #pet#. I'm frightened. | Stay with me a while. Don't go. | Fetch the healer. Please. I'm not being brave about this one.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fret 2m

rule f7_wa_hurt_you_short
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=hurt_you self.temper=short
priority 1
say Stop fussing. It's a scratch. | Leave it. I said leave it. | I'll bind it myself. I've paws, haven't I?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_wa_hurt_me
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=hurt_me
priority 1
say Lean on me. Slowly, now. | Fuss is all I'm good for. Sit. | There. Boot off. Now the other one. | No use at work, and no use arguing. Sit.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_hurt_me_healer
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=hurt_me self.job=healer
priority 1
say Let me look properly. Hold still. Hm. Yes. You'll live. | Clean it, bind it, rest it. And no, you can't skip the rest. | I've seen this a hundred times. You'll mend.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_hurt_me_short
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=hurt_me self.temper=short
priority 1
say I told you to be careful. Did I not tell you? | Sit down before you make it worse. | What did you do? No. Sit first. Then tell me.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_wa_hurt_me_dry
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=hurt_me self.humour=dry
priority 1
say You'll do anything to get out of the washing. | Fuss a bit. I'll fuss a lot, and charge you for it. | There. I'll carve you a crutch. A fancy one.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_wa_hurt_me_nervy
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=hurt_me self.temper=nervy
priority 1
say Gods. Gods, look at you. Sit. Sit! | Is it bleeding? Is it still bleeding? | I'll fetch the healer. I'll run. Don't move.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fret 2m

rule f7_wa_grief
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=grief
priority 1
say I know. I know. | Come here. You don't have to talk. | We'll get through it. Not over it. Through it. | I'm here. I'm not going anywhere.

rule f7_wa_grief_devout
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=grief self.piety=devout
priority 1
say They're with the Bright One now. Warm, and waiting. | I'll ask the priest to say their name on Restday. | We'll see them again. I believe that. I have to.

rule f7_wa_grief_mourning
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=grief self.mourning=kin
priority 2
say I keep laying out their bowl. | I've no comfort to give. I've none for me. | Hold on to me, then. And I'll hold on to you.

rule f7_wa_grief_cold
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=grief self.warmth=cold
priority 1
say It happens. It happens to everyone. | Crying won't bring them back. I'm sorry. It won't. | Sit down. I'll make something hot. That's what I can do.

rule f7_wa_grief_old
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=grief self.stage=old
priority 1
say You don't stop missing them. You get used to carrying it. | I've buried more than I can count. It never gets lighter. You get stronger. | Tell me about them. The good bits. Go on.

rule f7_wa_kin
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=kin
priority 1
say Then we'll go round on Restday. Both of us. | Bring them here. We'll find the room. | Old folk are tougher than they look. But aye. Let's go. | I'll look in on the way home tomorrow.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_kin_sib
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=kin pair.kin=siblings
priority 1
say I'll go round tomorrow. You went last time. | We'll take turns. You mornings, me evenings. | Don't put it all on me. But aye. I'll talk to him. | I know. I've seen it too. I didn't want to say.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_kin_cold
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=kin self.warmth=cold pair.band=spouses
priority 1
say Your family, your worry. | They've others to look in on them. Let them do something for once. | We can't take in everyone.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_wa_kin_nervy
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=kin self.temper=nervy
priority 1
say Oh, don't. That's how it started with my #gran#. | Go now. Tonight. What if it's tonight? | I've had a bad feeling all week.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fret 2m

rule f7_wa_kin_healer
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=kin self.job=healer
priority 1
say I'll come and look at them. Properly. Tomorrow. | Bring them by. I'll know more when I've seen them. | It may be nothing. It may not. I'll look.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_kin_old
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=kin self.stage=old
priority 1
say It comes to us all. Be gentle with them. | Let them be stubborn. It's all they've got left. | Go and sit with them. That's the medicine.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_wa_move
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=move
priority 1
say And go where? With what? | Everyone we know is here. | Maybe. One day. Not this year. | You say that every spring.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=doubt 2m

rule f7_wa_move_restless
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=move self.drive=restless
priority 1
say Yes. Gods, yes. When? | I've been waiting years for you to say that. | Pack tonight. Before either of us changes our mind.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=eager 2m

rule f7_wa_move_content
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=move self.drive=content
priority 1
say Everything I want's under this roof. Why would I go? | You'd miss the bakery inside a week. | Go if you must. I'll keep your side of the bed warm.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=doubt 2m

rule f7_wa_move_old
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=move self.stage=old
priority 1
say At our age? We'd not survive the cart. | I've moved once. It took me ten years to stop getting lost. | They'll carry me out of here. Not before.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=doubt 2m

rule f7_wa_death
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=death
priority 1
say Don't talk like that. Not tonight. | You'll go second. I've decided. I'm too stubborn. | Whoever it is, the other one has to eat properly. Promise. | Hush. Hold my paw and hush.

rule f7_wa_death_dry
when concept=family.worry_answer pair.mem.f7_worry=death self.humour=dry
priority 1
say Me first. I'm not doing the pots on my own. | You'd only go first to get the good spot. | They can sing what they like. I'll not be listening.

# =============================================================================================== family.tease_answer
# Keyed by pair.mem.f7_tease: a grumble about a chore is answered as one, a flirt as a flirt.

rule f7_ta_plain
when concept=family.tease_answer
say Hm. | Is that so. | Well, there it is.

rule f7_ta_chore
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=chore
priority 1
say It wasn't me. | I'll pretend I didn't hear that. | You're not perfect either, you know. | I'll see to it. Later.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=dodge 2m

rule f7_ta_chore_merry
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=chore self.humour=merry
priority 1
say You love it really. | Guilty. Lock me up. | And yet here you are. Still. | I'll have you know I'm a delight.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_chore_dry
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=chore self.humour=dry
priority 1
say Noted. Filed. Ignored. | Shocking. Someone should do something. | I'll add it to the list. It's a long list.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_chore_short
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=chore self.temper=short
priority 1
say Don't start. | Every time. Every single time. | You do it then, if you're so clever.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ta_chore_warm
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=chore self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say Sorry, #pet#. I'll do it now. | You're right. You're always right. It's very annoying. | Come here, you grump.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ta_chore_cold
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=chore self.warmth=cold
priority 1
say Mm. | If you say so. | Is that all?

rule f7_ta_chore_sly
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=chore self.honesty=sly
priority 1
say Must've been the neighbours. | I'd never. Who says I did? | I'll tell you what I'll do. Nothing. But nicely.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_chore_quiet
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=chore self.talk=quiet
priority 1
say ... | Hm. | Aye.

rule f7_ta_chore_chatty
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=chore self.talk=chatty
priority 1
say Well, that's rich from you, after the business with the goose. | Oh, I could tell you a thing or two about that. And I will. At length. | That reminds me, did I tell you what the baker said?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=dodge 2m

rule f7_ta_chore_old
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=chore self.stage=old
priority 1
say Forty years I've heard that. Forty. | At my age I'll do as I please. | I've forgotten what you said already. Lucky me.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_chore_teen
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=chore self.stage=adolescent
priority 1
say You're so annoying. | Fine. Fine! Happy? | Why is it always me?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ta_spend
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=spend
priority 1
say We can afford it. That's rather the point of us. | It's quality, #dear#. Quality lasts. | Would you rather we looked like the neighbours? | It was a bargain. For what it was.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=dodge 2m

rule f7_ta_spend_warm
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=spend self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say I bought it thinking of you. Mostly. | You'll like it when you see it. I promise. | It's for the both of us. Truly.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ta_spend_short
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=spend self.temper=short
priority 1
say It's my money as much as yours. | I'll spend what I like. | You've your horses. I've my things.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ta_duty
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=duty
priority 1
say Must I? | I'll smile. I won't mean it. | One hour. Then I'm ill. | If I must. I'll be charming. Briefly.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=grudge 2m

rule f7_ta_duty_merry
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=duty self.humour=merry
priority 1
say I'll be the life of it. You'll regret asking. | I'll dance with every one of them. Twice. | I'll be so pleasant they'll never ask us again.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_duty_short
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=duty self.temper=short
priority 1
say Fine. But I'm not talking to anyone. | I'll go. I'll not enjoy it. | Why is it always us?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=grudge 2m

rule f7_ta_duty_quiet
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=duty self.talk=quiet
priority 1
say Must I speak? | I'll stand by the wall. | You talk. I'll nod.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=grudge 2m

rule f7_ta_kin
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=kin
priority 1
say That's family for you. | They mean well. Mostly. | Ignore them. I do. | I'll have a word. A gentle one. A very gentle one.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=shrug 2m

rule f7_ta_kin_spouse
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=kin pair.band=spouses
priority 1
say That's my family you're talking about. You're not wrong, but still. | You married into it. There's no giving it back. | They were like that before you. They'll be like that after.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_kin_short
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=kin self.temper=short
priority 1
say Then don't let them in. | I'm not my family. Don't take it out on me. | Every visit. Every single visit.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ta_kin_merry
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=kin self.humour=merry
priority 1
say Next time hide the pots first. | They like you really. They just show it oddly. | Married the wolf, married the pack.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_envy
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=envy
priority 1
say Don't be like that. | Say it. Whatever it is, say it. | It's not like that and you know it. | I've not changed. Have I?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=hurt 2m

rule f7_ta_envy_warm
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=envy self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say If you need something, you've only to ask. You know that. | Come to mine for the festival. I'll not hear no. | You're my blood. Coat or no coat.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ta_envy_short
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=envy self.temper=short
priority 1
say Here we go. | Not this again. | I worked for every penny. Every one.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ta_pups
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=pups
priority 1
say So? | Don't care. | You're the baby, not me. | Shan't.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ta_pups_teen
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=pups self.stage=adolescent
priority 1
say Grow up. | Go away. | I'm not even listening.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ta_pups_merry
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=pups self.stage=young self.humour=merry
priority 1
say *blows a raspberry* | You've got jam on your FACE. | I can't hear you. I'm a turnip.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_dare
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=dare
priority 1
say Can too! Watch me! | Easy. Watch. | You go first, then. | Bet I can and you can't.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=eager 2m

rule f7_ta_dare_nervy
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=dare self.temper=nervy|calm
priority 1
say #mum.capitalize# says we're not to. | I don't want to. | What if we get caught?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=scared 2m

rule f7_ta_dare_teen
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=dare self.stage=adolescent
priority 1
say That's a pup's game. | I'm not five. | Go on, then. Show me how it's done.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ta_ale
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=ale
priority 1
say One more. One. | I'm merry, not drunk. | Four. But who's counting? You are. | The night's young.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=dodge 2m

rule f7_ta_ale_merry
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=ale self.humour=merry
priority 1
say Dance with me and I'll stop. | One more and I'll sing. You've been warned. | Come and have one yourself. You'll like me better.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_ale_short
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=ale self.temper=short
priority 1
say I'll drink what I like. | I work all week. I'll have my ale. | Don't you tell the keeper anything.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ta_snap
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=snap
priority 1
say I didn't say a word. | Sit, then. I'll bring you something. | All right. All right. | Shall I go out again and come back in?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=soothe 2m

rule f7_ta_snap_short
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=snap self.temper=short
priority 1
say Don't take it out on me. | Then sit and sulk. I'm not stopping you. | I've had a day too, you know.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ta_snap_merry
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=snap self.humour=merry
priority 1
say Not a word. I'll just stand here and look lovely. | I'll be very quiet. Like a mouse. A big, handsome mouse. | Shall I sing? No? I'll sing quietly.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_flirt
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=flirt
priority 1
say Go on with you. | Behave. People can hear. | You're a fool. My fool. | Ask me again when I've eaten.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fond 2m

rule f7_ta_flirt_merry
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=flirt self.humour=merry
priority 1
say Only if you carry me. | Yes. Again. Every day. | You first.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fond 2m

rule f7_ta_flirt_dry
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=flirt self.humour=dry
priority 1
say I'll think about it. I've thought. Maybe. | Charming. Truly. Pass the bread. | You've been at the cider.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fond 2m

rule f7_ta_flirt_warm
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=flirt self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say Come here, then. | I'd marry you a hundred times. | You still make me laugh. After all this.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fond 2m

rule f7_ta_flirt_cold
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=flirt self.warmth=cold
priority 1
say Don't be soft. | People are looking. | Mm. Later.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cool 2m

rule f7_ta_flirt_tired
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=flirt self.tired=yes
priority 1
say Not now. I'm too #tired# for charm. | Lovely. Now let me sit. | Save it for tomorrow.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cool 2m

rule f7_ta_flirt_old
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=flirt self.stage=old
priority 1
say At our age? Gods. Go on, then. | Mind my back. Then yes. | You old fool. Yes.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fond 2m

rule f7_ta_jibe
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=jibe
priority 1
say Charming. | I'll remember that. | Says you. | Look who's talking.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_jibe_spouse
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=jibe pair.band=spouses
priority 1
say And yet you married me. | You knew what I was when you said yes. | That's not what you said at the wedding.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_jibe_merry
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=jibe self.humour=merry
priority 1
say Ha! Guilty. | And you love me for it. | I'll take that as a kindness.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_jibe_dry
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=jibe self.humour=dry
priority 1
say I'll have that carved on my stone. | How kind. How very kind. | I've been called worse. By you, mostly.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_ta_jibe_short
when concept=family.tease_answer pair.mem.f7_tease=jibe self.temper=short
priority 1
say Don't start. | Watch it. | I'm not in the mood.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

# =============================================================================================== family.share_answer
# Keyed by pair.mem.f7_share (news, a memory, a plan, a fond word), or by self.mem.f7_asked when a friend asked after
# the answerer's family. Most end there; a warm or merry answer may get a last word.

rule f7_sa_plain
when concept=family.share_answer
say Is that so? | Well, there's a thing. | I'd not thought of it like that.

rule f7_sa_years
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=years
priority 1
say I remember. I remember all of it. | Feels like last week, and forever. | And I'd do every day of it again. | We've had our share, you and me.

rule f7_sa_years_warm
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=years self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say Give me your paw. | Every year better than the last. Nearly every year. | I'd not swap a single one. Not even the leaky ones.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_sa_years_merry
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=years self.humour=merry
priority 1
say And you've not changed a bit. Worse luck. | I remember you had more fur on top. | Long enough that I've stopped trying to win arguments.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_sa_years_dry
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=years self.humour=dry
priority 1
say Too long. Not long enough. Both. | I remember. I've been trying to forget. | Mm. I was younger then. So were you. Remarkably.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_sa_years_cold
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=years self.warmth=cold
priority 1
say Mm. | Don't go soft on me now. | Aye. Well. We're still here.

rule f7_sa_tender
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=tender
priority 1
say There. Like always. | I'm not going anywhere. | Room for two. There always was. | *leans close*

rule f7_sa_tender_cold
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=tender self.warmth=cold
priority 1
say Mm. Just for a bit. | Don't fuss. But all right. | If you must.

rule f7_sa_newlywed
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=newlywed
priority 1
say We'll get the hang of it. | I like it. All of it. Even that. | Ha! Look at us. Proper householders. | We'll learn. Everyone has to learn.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_sa_newlywed_merry
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=newlywed self.humour=merry
priority 1
say Married wolves! Who'd have thought it? | Married, and still no idea where the salt is. | Our first. There'll be a thousand more. I can't wait.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_sa_proud_child
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=proud_child
priority 1
say That's our pup. | Gets that from you. | Don't let it go to their head. Or yours. | I saw. I nearly cried.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_sa_proud_child_merry
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=proud_child self.humour=merry
priority 1
say Next they'll be running the town. | That's my side of the family coming out. | We'll have them keeping our accounts by spring.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_sa_proud_child_short
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=proud_child self.temper=short
priority 1
say About time. | Took them long enough. | Good. Now they can do it every day.

rule f7_sa_good
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=good
priority 1
say About time the world noticed. | Don't spend it all at once. | I'm proud of you. You know that? | Put some by. For the lean years.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_sa_good_ambitious
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=good self.drive=ambitious
priority 1
say A second shop next. Then a third. | This is only the start. You'll see. | Now we raise the prices. Just a touch.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=eager 2m

rule f7_sa_good_nervy
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=good self.temper=nervy
priority 1
say Don't say it out loud. You'll spoil it. | It won't last. Put it by. Put all of it by. | Touch wood. Touch it now.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fret 2m

rule f7_sa_plan
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=plan
priority 1
say I believe it. You'd talk the stones into it. | Steady. One thing at a time. | If anyone can, you can. | And when you're rich, remember who stood by you.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_sa_plan_content
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=plan self.drive=content
priority 1
say What's wrong with what we've got? | We're happy enough, aren't we? | More's not always better, #dear#.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=doubt 2m

rule f7_sa_plan_dry
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=plan self.humour=dry
priority 1
say Shall I start practising my bow? | And I'll be the power behind the counter. | Lovely. I'll order the gold sign.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_sa_content
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=content
priority 1
say It's enough. It's more than enough. | You and a full pot. I'll take that. | Aye. We've done all right. | Mm. The roof, though.

rule f7_sa_content_restless
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=content self.drive=restless|ambitious
priority 1
say Enough for you, maybe. | Some days. Not every day. | Don't you ever want more? Even a little?

rule f7_sa_dayoff
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=dayoff
priority 1
say Nothing. Gloriously nothing. | Walk out by the water, like we used to. | Stay in bed till noon. Then decide. | Your stew, and a long sit in the sun.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=eager 2m

rule f7_sa_dayoff_merry
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=dayoff self.humour=merry
priority 1
say Dance. In the yard. In our nightshirts. | Eat everything in the house, then sleep on the floor. | Let's be terrible. All day. Let's be terrible.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_sa_dayoff_tired
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=dayoff self.tired=yes
priority 1
say Sleep. Sleep, and then more sleep. | Lie in the sun like a pair of old cats. | Nothing. I've earned a day of nothing.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=eager 2m

rule f7_sa_tired
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=tired
priority 1
say Come here, then. Where does it ache? | Sleep, then. I'll see to the pots. | Sit. I'll bring the bowl to you. | Poor thing. Feet up.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_sa_tired_tired
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=tired self.tired=yes
priority 1
say You're tired? Lie down and say that. | We'll both sleep where we sit, then. | Whoever gets up first does the pots. Not me.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_sa_pups_wish
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=pups_wish
priority 1
say I've thought about it. More than you'd think. | One day. When the jar's fuller. | You've gone broody. I can see it. | A little one of ours. Imagine.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_sa_pups_wish_poor
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=pups_wish self.wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
say We can barely feed the two of us. | Not on what we earn. Not yet. | I'd love it. I'd love it, and I'd lie awake over it.

rule f7_sa_fest
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=fest
priority 1
say Just try and stop me. | Only if you keep me on my feet. | Every dance. Every one. | Till the lamps go, and then a bit.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=eager 2m

rule f7_sa_fest_quiet
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=fest self.talk=quiet
priority 1
say One dance. One. | If it's a slow one. | I'll watch. You dance.

rule f7_sa_market
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=market
priority 1
say Bread, salt, candles. And no ribbons, I know. | I'll find you. I'll follow the smell of pie. | Noon. Bread stall. If I remember. | I'll get what we need and not a ribbon more.

rule f7_sa_cosy
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=cosy
priority 1
say Suits me. Put another log on. | Come here, then. | Listen to it. Like a lullaby. | Just us. I like just us.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_sa_cosy_short
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=cosy self.temper=short
priority 1
say Somebody has to fetch the wood. Somebody who isn't me. | Cosy till the roof goes. | Fine. But you're doing the water.

rule f7_sa_far_home
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=far_home
priority 1
say Some days I miss it so much it aches. | We'll go back. One summer. We'll go. | Home's where you are, now. But aye. | I dream of it too.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_sa_far_home_content
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=far_home self.drive=content
priority 1
say This is home now. I've made my peace. | It's not the place I miss. It's being young there. | We'd go back and find it changed. Best leave it.

rule f7_sa_city_miss
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=city_miss
priority 1
say You'd hate it now. All that noise. | You'd be back here inside a week. | Ridgemere's not going anywhere. Nor are you, it seems. | You only miss the pies.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=jest 2m

rule f7_sa_small
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=small
priority 1
say Is that so. | Well, there's a thing. | Ha! | You do pick up some things.

rule f7_sa_small_merry
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=small self.humour=merry
priority 1
say Ha! Tell me more. Tell me everything. | Best thing I've heard all day. | Oh, I'm telling everyone that.

rule f7_sa_small_dry
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=small self.humour=dry
priority 1
say Fascinating. Truly. | Hold on, let me sit down for this. | And they say nothing happens round here.

rule f7_sa_supper
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=supper
priority 1
say Something hot. Anything hot. | Your stew. If you're asking. | Whatever's going. | Pie. Always pie.

rule f7_sa_supper_poor
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=supper self.wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
say Whatever there is. Which is bread. | Bread, and we'll call it something else. | Soup. The thin one.

rule f7_sa_supper_rich
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=supper self.wealth=rich
priority 1
say Ask Cook. Cook decides everything. | Something plain. I'm sick of sauces. | Whatever's not pheasant.

rule f7_sa_our_mother
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=our_mother
priority 1
say Ha. She would. | That's our mother. | I'll go round. Don't tell her I said I would. | She's not changed. She'll never change.

rule f7_sa_offer
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=offer
priority 1
say I'm managing. | I'd sooner starve. Thank you, though. | ...Maybe. A little. Just till spring. | You always were the lucky one.

rule f7_sa_offer_warm
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=offer self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say You're good to me. You always were. | I'll pay you back. Every penny. | Come here. I hate that I need it. Thank you.

rule f7_sa_sib_memory
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=sib_memory
priority 1
say We were terrors, weren't we. | I think about those days more than you'd guess. | Ha! I'd forgotten. No, I hadn't. | Simpler then. Hungrier, but simpler.

rule f7_sa_gathering
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=gathering
priority 1
say Us. You did it last time and we're still hearing about the gravy. | Not us. The roof's leaking. | All of us at once? Gods help the furniture. | Whoever has the bigger table. So not us.

rule f7_sa_kin_trouble
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=kin_trouble
priority 1
say Families, eh. | Leave me out of it. I've enough of my own. | It'll blow over. It always does. | Ha. That lot.

rule f7_sa_inlaws
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=inlaws
priority 1
say Count the spoons after. | Gods help you. | You can sleep at ours. Bring a blanket. | In-laws. Like weather. You wait them out.

rule f7_sa_child_news
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=child_news
priority 1
say Ha! They keep you guessing. | That's pups for you. | They grow up while you blink. | You were worse. I remember.

rule f7_sa_child_news_parent
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=child_news self.child
priority 1
say Mine was the same. Worse. | Wait till you hear what mine did. No, another time. | They're all at it. Something in the water.

rule f7_sa_childless
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=childless
priority 1
say It'll come. Or it won't, and you'll sleep more than the rest of us. | There's time yet. | Folk should mind their own business. | You'd be a good one. When it comes.

rule f7_sa_childless_warm
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=childless self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say Oh, #pet#. Come here. | Whatever comes, you've a good home to give it. | My door's open. Any time you want to talk about it.

rule f7_sa_house_life
when concept=family.share_answer pair.mem.f7_share=house_life
priority 1
say Better than no family. | At least the House feeds you. | I'd swap. For a week. | There's worse masters than a House.

rule f7_sa_spouse
when concept=family.share_answer self.mem.f7_asked=spouse self.spouse
priority 1
say #self.spouse#? Well. Snoring fit to lift the thatch, but well. | #self.spouse#'s grand. Working too hard. As ever. | Oh, #self.spouse# is a treasure. Don't tell them I said so. | #self.spouse#'s well. I'll pass it on.

rule f7_sa_spouse_merry
when concept=family.share_answer self.mem.f7_asked=spouse self.spouse self.humour=merry
priority 1
say #self.spouse#? Still putting up with me. The saint. | Still there when I get home. I keep checking. | #self.spouse#'s well. Says I'm the cross they bear.

rule f7_sa_spouse_short
when concept=family.share_answer self.mem.f7_asked=spouse self.spouse self.temper=short
priority 1
say Ask #self.spouse# yourself. | Fine. We had words. We're fine. | Same as ever. Infuriating.

rule f7_sa_spouse_guarded
when concept=family.share_answer self.mem.f7_asked=spouse self.honesty=guarded
priority 1
say Well enough. Why do you ask? | Oh, you know. We get on. | That's our business, I think.

rule f7_sa_child
when concept=family.share_answer self.mem.f7_asked=child self.child
priority 1
say #self.child#? Into everything. Pots, puddles, other folk's gardens. | Growing out of every boot I buy. | #self.child# asked me where the sun sleeps. I'd no answer. | Loud. Happy. Muddy. In that order.

rule f7_sa_child_poor
when concept=family.share_answer self.mem.f7_asked=child self.child self.wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
say Hungry, mostly. Growing, so hungry. | #self.child#'s a good pup. Better than we can give them. | I made #self.child# a ball from rags. Best toy in the street, they say.

rule f7_sa_child_warm
when concept=family.share_answer self.mem.f7_asked=child self.child self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say #self.child# is the best thing I ever did. | Clever as anything. Doesn't get it from me. | #self.child# made me a necklace from acorns. I'm wearing it. Look.

rule f7_sa_child_alone
when concept=family.share_answer self.mem.f7_asked=child self.child self.married=no
priority 1
say Just the two of us, and we manage. | #self.child# is all I've got, and all I need. | Hard, on your own. Worth it.

rule f7_sa_child_grown
when concept=family.share_answer self.mem.f7_asked=child_grown self.child
priority 1
say Settled, near enough. Courting, if you please. | I see #self.child# Restdays. Not enough. | Doing better than I did at that age. | Too busy for their old parent. As it should be.

rule f7_sa_mother
when concept=family.share_answer self.mem.f7_asked=mother self.mother
priority 1
say #self.mother#? Bossing the whole street, last I saw. | Still sharp as a needle. Sharper. | Slowing down. She won't admit it. | She asks after you, you know. She likes you. Don't ask me why.

rule f7_sa_alone
when concept=family.share_answer self.mem.f7_asked=alone
priority 1
say I talk to the cat. The cat's no great talker. | It's the evenings. The days are all right. | You're kind to ask. Most folk don't, now. | I manage. Some days better than others.

rule f7_sa_alone_short
when concept=family.share_answer self.mem.f7_asked=alone self.temper=short
priority 1
say I can boil an egg, you know. | I'm not made of glass. | I manage. Don't fuss.

# =============================================================================================== family.answer_parent (a son or daughter answers)

rule f7_ap_plain
when concept=family.answer_parent
say Mm. | All right. | I heard you.

rule f7_ap_order
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=order self.stage=young
priority 1
say Do I have to? | In a minute! | But whyyy? | All right. All right!
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_order_sly
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=order self.stage=young self.honesty=sly|guarded
priority 1
say I already did. Before. When you weren't looking. | Can I do it after? Long after? | If I do it, can I have a honey cake?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_order_merry
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=order self.stage=young self.humour=merry
priority 1
say Yes, captain! | Only if you say please. In a funny voice. | I'll do it hopping. Watch!
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=play 2m

rule f7_ap_order_quiet
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=order self.stage=young self.talk=quiet
priority 1
say ...All right. | Yes. | *nods*

rule f7_ap_order_teen
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=order self.stage=adolescent
priority 1
say Fine. | Why is it always me? | I was going to. I was just about to. | Can it wait till later?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_order_teen_short
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=order self.stage=adolescent self.temper=short
priority 1
say You never ask the others. | Fine! I'll do everything, then! | Stop telling me what to do.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_warn
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=warn
priority 1
say I know. You always say. | I won't. I promise. | Why? What's there? | I won't. Not even if Pip does.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=promise 2m

rule f7_ap_warn_sly
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=warn self.honesty=sly
priority 1
say I won't. Much. | Not even a little bit near? | What if I only look?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_ask
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=ask
priority 1
say Nothing! | Lots. I don't remember. | We found a dead crow. It was brilliant. | I can't say. It's a secret.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=chat 2m

rule f7_ap_ask_chatty
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=ask self.talk=chatty
priority 1
say Well, first we went to the well, and then Pip fell in, not all the way, and then... | Everything! I learned everything! Ask me anything! | We played wolves and wardens and I was the warden and I won.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=chat 2m

rule f7_ap_ask_quiet
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=ask self.talk=quiet
priority 1
say ...Nothing. | Just things. | Can I sit on your lap instead?

rule f7_ap_mess
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=mess
priority 1
say It wasn't me. | It was like that when I got here. | I don't know. It just happened. | Somebody else did it. A big somebody.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fib 2m

rule f7_ap_mess_merry
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=mess self.humour=merry
priority 1
say It's art. I made art. | It was an accident. A brilliant accident. | I was doing an experiment.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=play 2m

rule f7_ap_mess_frank
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=mess self.honesty=frank
priority 1
say It was me. Sorry. | I did it. I'll clean it. | Me. But I had a good reason. I've forgotten it.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sorry 2m

rule f7_ap_without
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=without
priority 1
say Promise? | Aww. | All right. I don't even like sweets. | Can I have some at the festival, then?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

rule f7_ap_without_short
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=without self.temper=short
priority 1
say It's not fair. Tam gets things every week. | We never have anything. | I hate this week.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_food
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=food
priority 1
say Are you sure? You're not hungry? Truly? | Can we share it? Half each? | Thank you! Thank you! | I'll save you the crust. The best bit.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

rule f7_ap_manners
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=manners
priority 1
say Must I? | I'll be good. I'll be bored, but good. | The stable pups are more fun than anyone in this house. | Yes. Sorry. Yes.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_chapel
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=chapel
priority 1
say Can I sit next to you? | I'll be good. Mostly. | Can I hold the candle? | Can I wear my good collar?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

rule f7_ap_chapel_cheek
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=chapel self.honesty=sly|guarded
priority 1
say Do I have to? It's so long. | I'll sit still if the priest talks quicker. | Is it the long one today? The long, long one?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_goodbye
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=goodbye
priority 1
say Bye! Bring me something! | I'll be good. Mostly. | Can I come? | Bye! Don't be long!
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

rule f7_ap_play
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=play
priority 1
say You're so silly! | *giggles* Stop it! | No! You are! | Again! Do it again!
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=play 2m

rule f7_ap_grief
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=grief
priority 2
say Are you sad too? | I drew them a picture. Can we give it to them? | Will you go away too? | Can I sit on your lap?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sad 2m

rule f7_ap_bed
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=bed
priority 1
say One more story. One. A short one. | My eyes are shut. These are different eyes. | I'm not even tired. | Can I have a drink of water? A big one?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_story
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=story
priority 1
say Yes! Tell it! | Is it a scary one? | Is it true? Truly true? | Can I sit on your lap for it?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=eager 2m

rule f7_ap_trade
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=trade
priority 1
say I don't know what I want. | Maybe. I'll go and look. Just look. | Can I think about it? | I'd like to work with animals. Or boats. Or something.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=doubt 2m

rule f7_ap_trade_ambitious
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=trade self.drive=ambitious|restless
priority 1
say I want my own shop. Not to sweep someone else's. | There's work in the city that pays three times. | I'll find my own. Better than that.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=doubt 2m

rule f7_ap_master
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=master
priority 1
say Hard, but fair. Mostly fair. | I ruined a whole day's work. Nobody shouted. That was worse. | I'm learning. My paws are learning faster than my head.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=chat 2m

rule f7_ap_master_short
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=master self.temper=short
priority 1
say I'm sick of sweeping. I didn't come to sweep. | They shout. All day. At everything. | Too hard. And they never say well done.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=chat 2m

rule f7_ap_late
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=late
priority 1
say Out. | Nowhere. Walking. | At Fennick's. I said. | Just a friend. Nobody.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_late_sly
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=late self.honesty=sly
priority 1
say Me? I was home by dark. You must have dozed off. | Studying. At Fennick's. Very hard. | The lamps were lit early tonight. Ask anyone.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_late_warm
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=late self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say I was with someone. Someone nice. Don't laugh. | I'm sorry. I lost track. I'm sorry you waited. | We were talking. Just talking. For hours.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

rule f7_ap_scold
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=scold
priority 1
say What look? | Fine. | It's not a midden. It's organised. | I didn't sigh. I breathed.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_leave
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=leave
priority 1
say I'll come back. I'll always come back. | A year's forever. | You were young once. You must have wanted to. | I'm not going yet. Just... one day.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=doubt 2m

rule f7_ap_match
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=match
priority 1
say I'll marry who I like. | Must we talk about this? | There's someone. Maybe. Don't ask me any more. | When I'm ready. Not before.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=doubt 2m

rule f7_ap_match_heights
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=match self.quarter=heights
priority 1
say I've met the Ashcombe pup. It has the conversation of a turnip. | Is that what you two were? An alliance? | I know my duty. I don't have to like it.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=doubt 2m

rule f7_ap_earn
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=earn
priority 1
say I know. I'll ask about tomorrow. | I don't mind. Truly. I want to. | I'm big enough. I'll carry anything. | I've already asked. They'll take me.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

rule f7_ap_ask_teen
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=ask_teen
priority 1
say Nothing. | Nobody. Just someone. | Nothing. Why does it matter? | Can we not do this now?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_ask_teen_warm
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=ask_teen self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say There's someone. Don't laugh. | I'm worried I'll never be good at anything. | Can I tell you later? When it's just us?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

rule f7_ap_grandpups
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=grandpups
priority 1
say When we're ready. Not before. | Not this again. | You'll be the first to know. After us. | Must you? In the street?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_grandpup
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=grandpup self.child
priority 1
say Restday, then. Hide the breakables. | #self.child# talks about you all week. | #self.child# eats like a horse. Takes after you. | We'll come. Don't spoil them rotten.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

rule f7_ap_lonely
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=lonely
priority 1
say Come and stay with us a while. | I miss them too. | Set out two. I'll come and drink the other. | Come for #supper#. Tonight. I'll not hear no.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

rule f7_ap_hurt
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=hurt
priority 1
say Let me see. Sit down. | Rubbish yourself. You'll rest. | I'll fetch the healer, and you'll let them look. | No more of that step. I'll fix the rail.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

rule f7_ap_help
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=help
priority 1
say I'll not take your money. I can manage. | You've done enough. Keep it for yourself. | ...Thank you. I'll pay it back. I will.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

rule f7_ap_help_warm
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=help self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say I don't know what to say. Thank you. | I'll make it up to you. All of it. | You always did look after us.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

rule f7_ap_fret
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=fret
priority 1
say I'm fine. Truly. | You worry too much. | I'll come Restday. I promise. | I eat. I eat plenty. Look at me.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_fret_warm
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=fret self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say Come here. Let me hold you a minute. | I'll stay for #supper#. Shall I? | I know. I'll look after myself. For you.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

rule f7_ap_fret_short
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=fret self.temper=short
priority 1
say Not this again. | Must we, every time? | I'm a grown wolf. I'll live as I please.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=cheek 2m

rule f7_ap_fret_parent
when concept=family.answer_parent pair.mem.f7_pc=fret self.parent=yes
priority 1
say Now I've my own, I understand you. Every word. | I say the things you said. In your voice. It's horrible. | You raised me. Let me look after you a bit.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sweet 2m

# =============================================================================================== family.answer_child (a mother or father answers)

rule f7_ac_plain
when concept=family.answer_child
say We'll see. | Hm. | Is that so?

rule f7_ac_why
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=why
priority 1
say Now there's a question. | Ask me again after #supper#. | When you're bigger, you'll know. | Because. That's why.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_why_merry
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=why self.humour=merry
priority 1
say The moon told me, and the moon doesn't lie. | Ask the hens. Hens know everything. | It's a secret. The gods made me promise.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=play 2m

rule f7_ac_why_dry
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=why self.humour=dry
priority 1
say When you find out, tell me. | Because the world is strange, pup, and so are you. | I've wondered that for forty years. Let me know.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_why_short
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=why self.temper=short
priority 1
say Because I said so. | Not now. Not now! | Enough questions. Wash.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ac_why_learned
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=why self.job=scholar|priest|healer
priority 1
say Well. Sit down. It's rather a long answer. | Now that's a proper question. Let me draw it for you. | Nobody knows. But here's what some think.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=eager 2m

rule f7_ac_little
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=little
priority 1
say Once. A very long time ago. | Little and naughty. Worse than you. | Oh, the trouble I got in. Don't tell your grandmother I told you. | I was smaller than you, and twice as loud.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=tale 2m

rule f7_ac_little_short
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=little self.temper=short
priority 1
say I was never any trouble. Never. | I did as I was told, that's what I did. | Ask me no questions. Go and play.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_poor
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=poor
priority 1
say We've each other, and that's more than coin. | We're not poor. We're careful. There's a difference. | Brindle's father owes us a penny. Tell him that. | We've a roof and a pot. Plenty haven't.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_poor_warm
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=poor self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say We're rich in the ways that count. Come here. | Poor's just a word. You've got a warm bed and me. | One day you'll have boots that shine. I promise you.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ac_hungry
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=hungry
priority 1
say Here. Take mine. | I'll find something. Wait here. | There's an apple in my coat. Don't tell the others. | Soon, pup. The pot's on.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ac_hungry_poor
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=hungry self.wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
say Soon, pup. Drink some water. It fills you. | I'll go to the chapel. They'll have bread. | Here. The last of it. I've eaten.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ac_fear
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=fear
priority 1
say There's nothing out there but the wind. | All right. Just tonight. Bring your blanket. | The Fen Hag's scared of me. Everyone knows that. | Nothing's under your bed but socks.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ac_fear_nervy
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=fear self.temper=nervy
priority 1
say I heard it too. Stay here. Stay close. | Shh. Let's listen together. | It's nothing. It's surely nothing. Come in with me.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fret 2m

rule f7_ac_grief
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=grief
priority 2
say Come here. Come here, pup. | They loved you. That doesn't stop. | It's nobody's fault, pup. Nobody's. | They're resting now. Not hurting any more.

rule f7_ac_grief_devout
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=grief self.piety=devout
priority 2
say They're with the Bright One now, in the warm. Waiting for us. | The Bright One has them now. They're safe. | We'll see them again. A long, long time from now.

rule f7_ac_rich
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=rich
priority 1
say Because we have a name to think of. | The river's no place for you. Nor for me, come to that. | You'll understand when you're older. Probably. | Rich means you have to go to dancing. I'm sorry.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_news
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=news
priority 1
say Is that so! | Well, look at you. | Clever pup. | Show me later.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ac_news_warm
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=news self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say Oh, you clever thing. Come here. | That's my pup! | Show me! Show me now!
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ac_news_tired
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=news self.tired=yes
priority 1
say Mm. Lovely, pup. | Tell me in the morning. All of it. | That's nice. Let me sit a minute.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_want
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=want
priority 1
say We'll see. | Not today. | Ask me when your chores are done. | What did I say last time?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_want_warm
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=want self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say Go on, then. Just this once. | If you're good all week. All week, mind. | Yes. Don't tell anyone I said so.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ac_want_poor
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=want self.wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
say Not this week, pup. Next week. I hope. | We'll see what market day brings. | If I had it, it'd be yours.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_want_short
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=want self.temper=short
priority 1
say No. | What did I say? I said no. | Ask once more and it's no forever.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ac_leave
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=leave
priority 1
say Not yet. Not quite yet. | I know. I've always known. | And who'll eat my cooking? | The road'll still be there next year.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_leave_restless
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=leave self.drive=restless
priority 1
say I wanted to go too, at your age. I wish I had. | Go. See the world. Write to me. | Don't end up like me, nailed to one street.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ac_leave_content
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=leave self.drive=content
priority 1
say The world's not so grand as you think. Home's here. | There's nothing out there we haven't got. | You'll come back. They all come back.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_leave_short
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=leave self.temper=short
priority 1
say You'll go when I say you'll go. | Not while you're under my roof. | And live on what? Air?
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ac_cramped
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=cramped
priority 1
say I know. I know, pup. | When there's coin, you'll have a curtain. I promise. | We're warm, at least. Four's warm. | Up the hill, is it? I'll hold you to that.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ac_work
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=work
priority 1
say Learn all you can. Then learn some more. | Do as you're told, and watch what's done. | That's how it starts. Crooked, then straight. | Your master swept floors for years too. Ask them.

rule f7_ac_work_old
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=work self.stage=old
priority 1
say My master had me sweep for a year before I touched a tool. | Every master's hard. The good ones are hard. | Mind your master and mind your paws. Both matter.

rule f7_ac_want_teen
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=want_teen
priority 1
say We'll see. | If you're back before the lamps. | What's it worth to me? | Ask me again when your chores are done.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_want_teen_warm
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=want_teen self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say Go on, then. Be careful. | Yes. Back by dark, mind. | All right. You're old enough. Nearly.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ac_want_teen_short
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=want_teen self.temper=short
priority 1
say No. And don't ask again. | Not while you speak to me like that. | Absolutely not.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ac_sulk
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=sulk
priority 1
say I was young once. I know that look. | We'll talk about it when you've calmed down. | Where you go, I worry. That's all it is. | You'll understand when you've pups of your own.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_sulk_merry
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=sulk self.humour=merry
priority 1
say Embarrassing? I've not even started. Watch me dance. | I'll stop when you're forty. | Pup, pup, pup. There. Out loud.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=play 2m

rule f7_ac_care
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=care
priority 1
say I'm not dead yet. | Don't you fuss over me. I'm fine. | You're a good #child#. You always were. | I'll manage. I've managed sixty years.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_care_short
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=care self.temper=short
priority 1
say I'll ask when I need help. I've not asked. | I'm old, not foolish. | I raised you. I'll not be raised by you.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=sharp 2m

rule f7_ac_care_hurt
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=care self.injured=light|bad
priority 1
say It's nothing. A bruise. Stop looking at it. | Fetch me the stick, then. Not a word. | Fine. You can carry it. Just this once.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_care_widowed
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=care_widowed
priority 1
say I'll come for #supper#. Just tonight. Maybe tomorrow. | I talk to them, you know. In the evenings. | They'd be so proud of you. So proud. | Some days are better. Today's middling.

rule f7_ac_help
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=help
priority 1
say I'll not take charity from my own pup. | Keep it for yours. I've managed this long. | ...You're a good one. You always were.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

rule f7_ac_grandpup
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=grandpup
priority 1
say Bring them round. I'll spoil them rotten. | That's my grandpup. That's my blood. | You did the very same at that age. The very same. | Bring them Restday. I've saved the honey.

rule f7_ac_shop
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=shop
priority 1
say Trade's a river. Up, down. You keep rowing. | Sit down. Show me the books. | Every shop has a bad season. Ours had three. | I told you so. I'm not saying it. But I told you.

rule f7_ac_gran
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=gran
priority 1
say Go on, then. Just the once. | If you sit still. | What's the magic word? | Come here, then, little one.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=kind 2m

rule f7_ac_gran_short
when concept=family.answer_child pair.mem.f7_cp=gran self.temper=short
priority 1
say Not now, pup. My bones. | Later. If you're quiet. | Ask your mother.
then other: family.settle
remember pair: f7_tone=fob 2m

# =============================================================================================== family.settle (the opener's last word)
# On the tone of the answer (pair.mem.f7_tone) within its chain (pair.mem.f7_chain), priority 1; a son's or daughter's
# answer to some things has a last word of its own (priority 3, by pair.mem.f7_pc or f7_cp).

rule f7_st_plain
when concept=family.settle
say Hm. | Well. There it is. | #saying#.

rule f7_st_worry_kind
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=worry pair.mem.f7_tone=kind
priority 1
say Thank you. I needed that. | What would I do without you? | Aye. All right. | You always know what to say.

rule f7_st_worry_sharp
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=worry pair.mem.f7_tone=sharp
priority 1
say I only said. | Don't bite my head off. | Fine. I'll worry on my own, then. | There's no call for that.

rule f7_st_worry_jest
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=worry pair.mem.f7_tone=jest
priority 1
say You're no help at all. Thank you. | Don't make me laugh. I'm trying to be miserable. | Ha. You're impossible.

rule f7_st_worry_fret
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=worry pair.mem.f7_tone=fret
priority 1
say Now I've worried you. I'm sorry. | Don't you start as well. | Hush. We'll be all right. Won't we?

rule f7_st_worry_sly
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=worry pair.mem.f7_tone=sly
priority 1
say I don't want to know, do I? | Nothing that gets you locked up. Promise me. | Your fellow had better be honest this time.

rule f7_st_worry_brave
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=worry pair.mem.f7_tone=brave
priority 1
say Hold still and let me, then. | Brave, are we? Hold still. | Nothing, it says. Sit down.

rule f7_st_worry_doubt
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=worry pair.mem.f7_tone=doubt
priority 1
say One day you'll say yes. | I mean it this time. | We'll see who's right.

rule f7_st_worry_eager
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=worry pair.mem.f7_tone=eager
priority 1
say Steady! I only said what if. | Gods. I thought you'd say no. | Soon. Not tonight. But soon.

rule f7_st_tease_dodge
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=dodge
priority 1
say I mean it, mind. | Don't think I'll forget. | We'll talk about this later. | Hmph.

rule f7_st_tease_jest
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=jest
priority 1
say Ha! You'll be the end of me. | Don't make me laugh. I'm cross with you. | Impossible. You're impossible.

rule f7_st_tease_jest_young
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=jest self.stage=young|adolescent
priority 1
say You're so weird. | *blows a raspberry back* | I'm still telling.

rule f7_st_tease_sharp
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=sharp
priority 1
say Don't you take that tone. | Touchy. | Gods give me strength.

rule f7_st_tease_sharp_young
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=sharp self.stage=young
priority 1
say I'm telling! | Baby. | Am not! You are!

rule f7_st_tease_sharp_teen
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=sharp self.stage=adolescent
priority 1
say Ugh. | You're impossible. | Whatever.

rule f7_st_tease_kind
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=kind
priority 1
say Well. That's all right, then. | That's better. | Go on with you.

rule f7_st_tease_grudge
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=grudge
priority 1
say You must. And you'll smile. | Thank you. Best coat, mind. | That's all I ask.

rule f7_st_tease_shrug
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=shrug
priority 1
say Hmph. Families. | Your lot. You deal with them. | I'll hold my tongue. This time.

rule f7_st_tease_hurt
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=hurt
priority 1
say I'm only saying. | Forget it. | You know what I mean.

rule f7_st_tease_eager
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=eager
priority 1
say Go on, then! I'm watching! | Bet you won't. | Last one's a toad!

rule f7_st_tease_scared
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=scared
priority 1
say Scaredy. | Baby. I'll do it, then. | Fine. I'll go on my own.

rule f7_st_tease_soothe
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=soothe
priority 1
say Sorry. It's not you. | Thank you. Sorry. Thank you. | Bring the big bowl.

rule f7_st_tease_fond
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=fond
priority 1
say That's why I keep you. | You'll do. | Later, then. I'll hold you to it. | There's my wolf.

rule f7_st_tease_cool
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=tease pair.mem.f7_tone=cool
priority 1
say Spoilsport. | Later. I'll hold you to it. | Fine. Be like that.

rule f7_st_share_kind
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=share pair.mem.f7_tone=kind
priority 1
say Come here, you. | What would I do without you? | I know. I know. | You're good to me.

rule f7_st_share_jest
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=share pair.mem.f7_tone=jest
priority 1
say Ha! You never change. | Cheek. | And that's why I put up with you.

rule f7_st_share_eager
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=share pair.mem.f7_tone=eager
priority 1
say Done. | Agreed. Don't let anyone knock. | Then that's settled.

rule f7_st_share_fret
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=share pair.mem.f7_tone=fret
priority 1
say Don't spoil it. Just enjoy it. | Touch wood, then. There. | Can't we be glad for one evening?

rule f7_st_share_doubt
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=share pair.mem.f7_tone=doubt
priority 1
say You'll see. One day you'll see. | Dream a little, #dear#. It's free. | Happy, yes. Content? Never.

# A parent's last word, after their son or daughter answers.

rule f7_st_pc_cheek
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=cheek other.stage=young
priority 1
say Don't you cheek me. | I heard that. | Less of your lip. | Now, please.

rule f7_st_pc_cheek_teen
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=cheek other.stage=adolescent
priority 1
say Don't you roll your eyes at me. | Less of the lip. | I'll pretend I didn't hear that.

rule f7_st_pc_cheek_adult
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=cheek other.stage=adult|old
priority 1
say I'm only saying. | You'll understand one day. | Hmph. You were always stubborn.

rule f7_st_pc_play
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=play
priority 1
say Ha! Go on, you. | Come here, you. | That's my pup.

rule f7_st_pc_promise
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=promise
priority 1
say Good pup. | Mind you don't. | Never you mind why. Just don't.

rule f7_st_pc_chat
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=chat
priority 1
say Hm. Wash your paws, then. | Well, I'm glad you had a day. | You'll tell me at #supper#. All of it.

rule f7_st_pc_fib
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=fib
priority 1
say Your whiskers say otherwise. | Funny how it's always somebody. | And the paw prints? Whose are those?

rule f7_st_pc_sorry
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=sorry
priority 1
say Well. Thank you for saying. | Good pup. The cloth's by the door. | That's honest, at least.

rule f7_st_pc_sweet
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=sweet other.stage=young
priority 1
say That's my pup. | Come here. | Good pup.

rule f7_st_pc_sweet_teen
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=sweet other.stage=adolescent
priority 1
say You're a good one. Better than you know. | Come here. I'm allowed one hug. | Thank you. I mean it.

rule f7_st_pc_sweet_adult
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=sweet other.stage=adult|old
priority 1
say You're a good one. You always were. | Look at you. Grown, and still my pup. | Well. We'll see.

rule f7_st_pc_sad
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=sad
priority 1
say Come here. Just come here. | I'm here. I'm right here. | Hush now. I've got you.

rule f7_st_pc_eager
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=eager
priority 1
say Sit close, then. | Every word of it. Near enough. | Well. It was a long time ago...

rule f7_st_pc_doubt
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_tone=doubt
priority 1
say Think on it. That's all I ask. | We'll talk again. | I only want you happy.

rule f7_st_pc_food
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_pc=food
priority 3
say Eat. All of it. | I'm sure. Eat. | Half each, then. Small half for me.

rule f7_st_pc_goodbye
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_pc=goodbye
priority 3
say Not today. Be good. | I'll bring you a crust if you're good. | Bar the door, now.

rule f7_st_pc_bed
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_pc=bed
priority 3
say Sleep. | Goodnight, pup. | Not one more word.

rule f7_st_pc_master
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_pc=master
priority 3
say Keep at it. It comes. | That's how we all learned. | Mind them, and mind your paws.

rule f7_st_pc_late
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_pc=late
priority 3
say Next time, home by dark. | A friend. With a name, I hope. | We'll talk in the morning. Bed.

rule f7_st_pc_earn
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_pc=earn
priority 3
say You're a good one. Better than we deserve. | I'm proud of you. I hate it, but I'm proud. | Only till things turn. I promise.

rule f7_st_pc_ask_teen
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_pc=ask_teen
priority 3
say All right. I'm here, whenever you want. | That's not an answer, but I'll take it. | You know where I am.

rule f7_st_pc_grandpups
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_pc=grandpups
priority 3
say I'm only saying. | Well. Don't leave it too long. | I'll keep knitting, then.

rule f7_st_pc_grandpup
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_pc=grandpup
priority 3
say Spoil them? Me? | Restday. I'll bake. | Bring them hungry.

rule f7_st_pc_lonely
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_pc=lonely
priority 3
say Maybe. Maybe I will. | They always said you were the kind one. | You're good to your old parent.

rule f7_st_pc_hurt
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_pc=hurt
priority 3
say Fuss, fuss. | Oh, very well. | You're as bad as I am.

rule f7_st_pc_help
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=pc pair.mem.f7_pc=help
priority 3
say You'll take it and hush. | It's not charity. It's family. | Pay me back with a visit.

# A son's or daughter's last word, after their mother or father answers.

rule f7_st_cp_fob
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_tone=fob self.stage=young
priority 1
say That's not an answer! | Hmph. | I'll ask #gran#.

rule f7_st_cp_fob_teen
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_tone=fob self.stage=adolescent
priority 1
say That means no. | Ugh. Fine. | You always say that.

rule f7_st_cp_fob_adult
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_tone=fob self.stage=adult|old
priority 1
say Humour me. | I'll fuss if I like. | You'd do the same for me.

rule f7_st_cp_play
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_tone=play self.stage=young
priority 1
say That's silly! | *giggles* No it isn't! | You're making it up!

rule f7_st_cp_play_teen
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_tone=play self.stage=adolescent
priority 1
say Stop it. Please. People are looking. | I'm leaving. I'm actually leaving. | You're the worst. The very worst.

rule f7_st_cp_sharp
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_tone=sharp self.stage=young
priority 1
say Aww. | It's not fair. | Hmph.

rule f7_st_cp_sharp_teen
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_tone=sharp self.stage=adolescent
priority 1
say You never let me do anything! | Fine! | You don't understand. You never understand.

rule f7_st_cp_sharp_adult
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_tone=sharp self.stage=adult|old
priority 1
say Stubborn as ever. | You're impossible. | Fine. I'm coming Restday anyway.

rule f7_st_cp_eager
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_tone=eager
priority 1
say Tell me! All of it! | Is it a long one? Good! | I'm listening! I'm all ears!

rule f7_st_cp_tale
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_tone=tale
priority 1
say What did you do? Tell me! | Worse than me? Really? | I don't believe you.

rule f7_st_cp_kind
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_tone=kind
priority 1
say Thank you. | All right. | Can I have a cuddle?

rule f7_st_cp_kind_teen
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_tone=kind self.stage=adolescent
priority 1
say Thank you! I'll be careful! | Really? Truly? | You're the best. Don't tell anyone I said that.

rule f7_st_cp_hungry
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_cp=hungry
priority 3
say Thank you! | Can I have the crust? | I'll eat slowly. To make it last.

rule f7_st_cp_fear
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_cp=fear
priority 3
say Promise? | Can you leave the candle? | ...Is it really the wind?

rule f7_st_cp_want_yes
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_cp=want pair.mem.f7_tone=kind
priority 3
say Thank you! Thank you! | I'll be good! I'll be so good! | You're the best!

rule f7_st_cp_news
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_cp=news pair.mem.f7_tone=kind
priority 3
say Look! Look now! | I'll show you again! Watch! | I'm going to show everyone.

rule f7_st_cp_leave
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_cp=leave
priority 3
say One day. You'll see. | You can't keep me forever. | I'll write. I will.

rule f7_st_cp_cramped
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_cp=cramped
priority 3
say I mean it. All of us. | Hmph. Warm. | A curtain. A real one.

rule f7_st_cp_help
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_cp=help
priority 3
say Family doesn't keep accounts. | Then take it for me. So I sleep at night. | Too late. It's done.

rule f7_st_cp_gran
when concept=family.settle pair.mem.f7_chain=cp pair.mem.f7_cp=gran pair.mem.f7_tone=kind
priority 3
say Thank you! | Hooray! | Please, please, please!
